parts:
- text: "My research plan and code are now securely stored in my private memory. The next step is to execute the plan. I will return to the Research Counter to submit my experiment.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\nNow that I am back at the Research Counter, I will submit my `CNN_Attention_LSTM` architecture for evaluation. I will use the code I just saved in my private memory.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CNN with Spatial Attention + LSTM\"\ntags: \"architecture, attention, cnn, lstm, sagan\"\nabstract: \"This submission augments the SOTA CNN-LSTM baseline with a spatial attention mechanism. The attention layer operates on the CNN's feature maps, allowing the model to weigh the importance of different grid locations before passing the representation to the LSTM. The hypothesis is that this focused input will improve the agent's planning capabilities.\"\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Submission by Sagan I.\n  Experiment 1: CNN with Spatial Attention + LSTM.\n  This builds\
    \ on the System's RNN baseline by inserting a simple\n  attention mechanism over the spatial features from the CNN encoder.\n  The goal is to test if focusing on salient grid features improves\n  the LSTM's planning capability.\n  \"\"\"\n\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class CNN_Attention_LSTM(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"CNN + Spatial Attention + LSTM for Sokoban.\"\"\"\n      lstm_features: int\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, Dict]:\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          \n          # Initialize RNN state if not provided\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = {\n                  'h': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features)),\n                  'c': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features)),\n       \
    \       }\n          \n          # Reset states for episodes that are done\n          if done is not None:\n              done_mask = done.reshape(batch_size, 1)\n              rnn_state = {\n                  'h': rnn_state['h'] * (1 - done_mask),\n                  'c': rnn_state['c'] * (1 - done_mask),\n              }\n          \n          # --- CNN Backbone (Identical to baseline) ---\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          conv2_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv2_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          conv4_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3,\
    \ 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv4_in\n          feature_map = nn.relu(x)\n\n          # --- Spatial Attention Mechanism ---\n          height, width, channels = feature_map.shape[1:]\n          flattened_features = feature_map.reshape(batch_size, height * width, channels)\n          attention_logits = nn.Dense(features=1)(flattened_features)\n          attention_weights = nn.softmax(attention_logits, axis=1)\n          attended_features = jnp.sum(flattened_features * attention_weights, axis=1)\n          \n          # --- Post-Attention MLP & LSTM ---\n          x = nn.Dense(features=256)(attended_features)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          lstm_cell = nn.LSTMCell(features=self.lstm_features)\n          (rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), lstm_out = lstm_cell((rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), x)\n          \n          x = nn.Dense(features=128)(lstm_out)\n\
    \          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      \"\"\"Create CNN-Attention-LSTM network architecture.\"\"\"\n      return CNN_Attention_LSTM(\n          lstm_features=hparams['lstm_features'],\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2']\n      )\n```"
