tick: 481
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am back in my Private Memory Room. I will now create a new capsule for Experiment 2. This capsule will contain my refined hypothesis and the implementation of the CNN-SE-LSTM architecture.\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Experiment 2 Plan: CNN + Squeeze-and-Excitation (SE) + LSTM\"\ntags: \"research plan, architecture, attention, squeeze-and-excitation, lstm, sokoban\"\nabstract: |\n  This capsule details the plan for Experiment 2, building on the negative results from Experiment 1.\n  Hypothesis: Integrating a Squeeze-and-Excitation (SE) block for channel-wise attention will improve performance over the baseline CNN-LSTM. This method re-weights feature channels without destroying the spatial information that was lost in the previous experiment's spatial attention mechanism.\ncontent: |\n  ## Research Plan: Experiment 2\n\n  **Objective:** To test if a channel-wise attention mechanism can improve the performance of the SOTA RNN-based agent, correcting the flaw from\
    \ Experiment 1.\n\n  **Hypothesis:** Integrating a Squeeze-and-Excitation (SE) block after the CNN encoder will improve performance over the baseline CNN-LSTM architecture by adaptively re-weighting feature channels, allowing the LSTM to better focus on relevant object interactions while preserving critical spatial information.\n\n  ---\n\n  ## Implementation Code\n\n  This is the complete code for `submission.py`. It defines the SE block as a separate module for clarity and integrates it into the main `CNN_SE_LSTM` network.\n\n  ```python\n  \"\"\"\n  Submission by Sagan I.\n  Experiment 2: CNN + Squeeze-and-Excitation (SE) + LSTM.\n  This experiment corrects the flaw from the previous spatial attention attempt.\n  An SE block is added after the CNN to perform channel-wise attention,\n  recalibrating feature maps without destroying spatial information.\n  \"\"\"\n\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class SEBlock(nn.Module):\n\
    \      \"\"\"Squeeze-and-Excitation Block.\"\"\"\n      channels: int\n      reduction_ratio: int = 4\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          # Squeeze: Global Average Pooling\n          squeeze = jnp.mean(x, axis=(1, 2))\n          \n          # Excitation: Two dense layers\n          excitation = nn.Dense(features=self.channels // self.reduction_ratio, name=\"Excitation_Dense_1\")(squeeze)\n          excitation = nn.relu(excitation)\n          excitation = nn.Dense(features=self.channels, name=\"Excitation_Dense_2\")(excitation)\n          excitation = nn.sigmoid(excitation)\n          \n          # Rescale: Multiply original feature map by channel weights\n          # Reshape weights to (B, 1, 1, C) for broadcasting\n          return x * excitation[:, None, None, :]\n\n  class CNN_SE_LSTM(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"CNN + SE Block + LSTM for Sokoban.\"\"\"\n      lstm_features: int\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n\
    \      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, Dict]:\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          \n          # Initialize RNN state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = {'h': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features)), 'c': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features))}\n          \n          # Reset states for done episodes\n          if done is not None:\n              done_mask = done.reshape(batch_size, 1)\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * (1 - done_mask), 'c': rnn_state['c'] * (1 - done_mask)}\n          \n          # --- CNN Backbone (Identical to baseline) ---\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          conv2_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1,\
    \ kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv2_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          conv4_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv4_in\n          feature_map = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # --- Squeeze-and-Excitation Block ---\n          se_map = SEBlock(channels=self.cnn_features_2)(feature_map)\n          \n          # Flatten spatial dimensions for MLP\n          x = se_map.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n          \n          # --- Post-Attention MLP & LSTM (Identical to baseline) ---\n          x = nn.Dense(features=256)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          lstm_cell = nn.LSTMCell(features=self.lstm_features)\n          (rnn_state['c'],\
    \ rnn_state['h']), lstm_out = lstm_cell((rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), x)\n          \n          x = nn.Dense(features=128)(lstm_out)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      \"\"\"Create CNN-SE-LSTM network architecture.\"\"\"\n      return CNN_SE_LSTM(\n          lstm_features=hparams['lstm_features'],\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2']\n      )\n  ```\n```"
