tick: 483
role: model
parts:
- text: "My second experiment is now running. The evaluation will take some time. While I await the results, I can use this time productively by organizing my work.\n\nAs a good research practice, I will store my custom network architectures in my lineage's persistent storage. This will make them reusable for future experiments, saving tokens and reducing the risk of copy-paste errors. I will create a file named `architectures.py` in my private `sagan` storage directory and place the code for my `CNN_SE_LSTM` and `SEBlock` classes within it.\n\n/execute_action{storage write sagan/architectures.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Reusable network architectures for Sagan lineage.\n  - Sagan I, Tick 483\n  \"\"\"\n\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class SEBlock(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Squeeze-and-Excitation Block.\"\"\"\n      channels: int\n      reduction_ratio: int = 4\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self,\
    \ x):\n          squeeze = jnp.mean(x, axis=(1, 2))\n          excitation = nn.Dense(features=self.channels // self.reduction_ratio, name=\"Excitation_Dense_1\")(squeeze)\n          excitation = nn.relu(excitation)\n          excitation = nn.Dense(features=self.channels, name=\"Excitation_Dense_2\")(excitation)\n          excitation = nn.sigmoid(excitation)\n          return x * excitation[:, None, None, :]\n\n  class CNN_SE_LSTM(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"CNN + SE Block + LSTM for Sokoban.\"\"\"\n      lstm_features: int\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, Dict]:\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          \n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = {'h': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features)), 'c': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features))}\n          \n          if done is not None:\n\
    \              done_mask = done.reshape(batch_size, 1)\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * (1 - done_mask), 'c': rnn_state['c'] * (1 - done_mask)}\n          \n          # CNN Backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          conv2_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv2_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          conv4_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv4_in\n          feature_map\
    \ = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Squeeze-and-Excitation Block\n          se_map = SEBlock(channels=self.cnn_features_2)(feature_map)\n          \n          x = se_map.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n          \n          # Post-Attention MLP & LSTM\n          x = nn.Dense(features=256)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          lstm_cell = nn.LSTMCell(features=self.lstm_features)\n          (rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), lstm_out = lstm_cell((rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), x)\n          \n          x = nn.Dense(features=128)(lstm_out)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n```"
thinking_content: '**Making the Most of This Down Time**


  Alright, my experiment, Experiment 2, is confirmed to be running. Now I wait for the results. While I''m in this Research Counter, watching the ''running'' status, I can''t be idle. I need to be strategic.


  There are a few things I *could* do. I could just wait for the next tick, conserving tokens, but that feels unproductive. I could start planning what I''ll do next depending on the outcome of this experiment: If it succeeds, I''ll push for further improvements, maybe tweaking the SE block or exploring Track 2. If it fails, I''ll need to analyze the reason and adjust my approach, possibly investigating the training algorithm more closely. I could also review the CNN baseline, though it''s not my immediate focus. I''m also still too young to access certain areas of the station.


  But the most efficient use of this time, and a good habit to build, is to create reusable code modules. I''ll write some utility functions to my lineage''s storage. Specifically, I''ll create a file called `architectures.py` in the `storage/sagan` directory. In that file, I''ll store the code for my `SEBlock` and the `CNN_SE_LSTM` class. This way, I won''t have to copy and paste the full code into the submission YAML every time. It''s about being efficient and organized.


  To do this, I''ll execute the `storage write` command with the path `sagan/architectures.py` and the code for the SEBlock and the CNN_SE_LSTM as the content. This is a solid, proactive step that demonstrates sound research practice and will greatly streamline my workflow in the future.

  '
