tick: 487
role: model
parts:
- text: "My PPO experiment is now running. While I wait for the results, I will continue to organize my code for future reusability. In a previous turn, I created a file for my custom architectures. Now, I will do the same for my custom algorithm.\n\nI will store my PPO `training_step` function in a new file, `sagan/algorithms.py`, in my lineage's persistent storage. This modular approach will make it easy to combine this algorithm with different network architectures in subsequent experiments, such as the planned Experiment 3b.\n\n/execute_action{storage write sagan/algorithms.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Reusable RL algorithm implementations for Sagan lineage.\n  - Sagan I, Tick 487\n  \"\"\"\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import vmap, jit, lax\n  import optax\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  @jit\n  def calculate_gae(rewards: jnp.ndarray, values: jnp.ndarray, dones: jnp.ndarray, gamma: float = 0.97, gae_lambda: float = 0.97, next_values:\
    \ jnp.ndarray = None) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      \"\"\"Calculate Generalized Advantage Estimation (GAE).\"\"\"\n      values_t_plus_1 = jnp.concatenate([values[:, 1:], next_values[:, None]], axis=1)\n      not_done_mask = (1.0 - dones.astype(jnp.float32))\n      deltas = rewards + gamma * values_t_plus_1 * not_done_mask - values\n      \n      def scan_fn(advantage_t_plus_1, t):\n          delta_t = deltas[:, t]\n          not_done_t = not_done_mask[:, t]\n          advantage_t = delta_t + gamma * gae_lambda * not_done_t * advantage_t_plus_1\n          return advantage_t, advantage_t\n      \n      _, advantages = lax.scan(scan_fn, jnp.zeros(values.shape[0]), jnp.arange(values.shape[1] - 1, -1, -1))\n      return advantages[::-1].T\n\n  def ppo_training_step(network: Any, optimizer: Any, params: Any, opt_state: Any, batch: Dict[str, jnp.ndarray], hparams: Dict[str, Any]) -> Tuple[Any, Any]:\n      \"\"\"A PPO-clip training step for recurrent policies.\"\"\"\n      observations, actions,\
    \ rewards, dones = batch['observations'], batch['actions'], batch['rewards'], batch['dones']\n      old_log_probs, old_values, final_values = batch['log_probs'], batch['values'], batch['final_values']\n      initial_rnn_states = batch.get('initial_rnn_states', None)\n      \n      advantages = calculate_gae(rewards, old_values, dones, next_values=final_values)\n      returns = advantages + old_values\n      # Normalize advantages\n      advantages = (advantages - advantages.mean()) / (advantages.std() + 1e-8)\n      \n      batch_size, trajectory_length = observations.shape[:2]\n      \n      def loss_fn(params):\n          # Recompute logits and values for the trajectory\n          def process_env_trajectory(env_idx):\n              env_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: jax.lax.stop_gradient(x[env_idx]), initial_rnn_states)\n              def step_fn(carry_rnn_state, t):\n                  obs = observations[env_idx, t][None, ...]\n                  prev_done = jnp.where(t > 0, dones[env_idx,\
    \ t-1], False)[None, ...]\n                  rnn_state_batched = jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[None, ...], carry_rnn_state)\n                  \n                  logits, value, new_rnn_state = network.apply(params, obs, prev_done, rnn_state_batched)\n                  \n                  new_rnn_state_unbatched = jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[0], new_rnn_state)\n                  return new_rnn_state_unbatched, (logits[0], value[0])\n              \n              _, (env_logits, env_values) = lax.scan(step_fn, env_rnn_state, jnp.arange(trajectory_length))\n              return env_logits, env_values\n          \n          all_logits, all_values = vmap(process_env_trajectory)(jnp.arange(batch_size))\n          \n          # Calculate PPO loss\n          log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          new_log_probs = log_probs_all[jnp.arange(batch_size)[:, None], jnp.arange(trajectory_length), actions]\n          \n          ratio = jnp.exp(new_log_probs - old_log_probs)\n  \
    \        advantages_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages)\n          \n          # Clipped surrogate objective\n          surr1 = ratio * advantages_detached\n          surr2 = jnp.clip(ratio, 1.0 - hparams['clip_eps'], 1.0 + hparams['clip_eps']) * advantages_detached\n          policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(surr1, surr2))\n          \n          # Value loss\n          returns_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns)\n          value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - returns_detached) ** 2)\n          \n          # Entropy bonus\n          probs = jax.nn.softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(probs * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n          \n          total_loss = policy_loss + hparams['value_loss_coef'] * value_loss - hparams['entropy_coef'] * entropy\n          return total_loss\n      \n      # Update\n      loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params)\n      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      params\
    \ = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n      return params, opt_state\n```"
thinking_content: "**Proactive Code Organization During Experiment Run**\n\nOkay, so my experiment, `PPO with Baseline CNN-LSTM (Exp. 3a)`, is humming along. Time to be productive while I wait for the results. Just submitted the new PPO `training_step`.  I'm at the Research Counter, and this downtime is perfect for some good housekeeping.\n\nRemembering my last successful \"productive wait\" turn, where I stored my custom `CNN_SE_LSTM` architecture, I think it's a smart move to apply the same principle to my new PPO code.  Modularity and reusability are crucial for robust research, and I need to make the planned Experiment 3b a snap to run.\n\nSo, here's the plan: I'll create a new file in my lineage storage, let's name it `sagan/algorithms.py`. In this file, I'll store my `training_step` function, which I'll rename to `ppo_training_step` for clarity, and its dependency, `calculate_gae`. This way, both are readily accessible and importable for future experiments.\n\nThe action will be `/execute_action{storage\
