tick: 489
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am back in the Private Memory Room. My last experiment failed because my PPO implementation was flawed. I will now design Experiment 4, which will feature a corrected, multi-epoch PPO implementation. This is a critical step in my research on algorithmic improvements.\n\nI will create a new capsule to document this refined approach.\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Experiment 4 Plan: Multi-Epoch PPO\"\ntags: \"research plan, algorithm, ppo, multi-epoch, sokoban\"\nabstract: |\n  This capsule details the plan for Experiment 4, a corrected implementation of PPO.\n  Hypothesis: My previous PPO experiment failed due to performing only a single gradient update per trajectory. A corrected, multi-epoch PPO that performs multiple updates on each batch of experience will more effectively stabilize training and surpass the baseline's performance.\n  Method: The `training_step` will be rewritten to include an inner loop for multiple training epochs and mini-batching.\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  ## Research Plan: Experiment 4 - Multi-Epoch PPO\n\n  **Objective:** To implement and test a canonical version of PPO featuring multiple training epochs and mini-batching over each collected trajectory.\n\n  **Hypothesis:** The failure of Experiment 3a was due to an incorrect, single-update implementation. A multi-epoch PPO implementation will align with established best practices, leading to better data utilization, more stable policy updates, and a final score superior to the baseline policy gradient method.\n\n  **Experimental Series:**\n  1.  **Experiment 4a:** Implement the multi-epoch PPO `training_step` with the baseline `CNNLSTM` architecture. This will be a direct, controlled test of the corrected algorithm.\n  2.  **Experiment 4b (Conditional):** If 4a is successful, combine the multi-epoch PPO `training_step` with my `CNN_SE_LSTM` architecture.\n\n  ---\n\n  ## Multi-Epoch PPO Implementation Code (for Experiment 4a)\n\n  This code for `submission.py` implements the\
    \ corrected PPO algorithm. It includes new hyperparameters for the number of epochs and mini-batches. It uses the `sagan/architectures.py` file to load the SOTA `CNNLSTM` model.\n\n  ```python\n  \"\"\"\n  Submission by Sagan I.\n  Experiment 4a: Multi-Epoch PPO with baseline RNN.\n  This is a corrected PPO implementation that performs multiple gradient\n  updates per collected trajectory, which is standard practice.\n  \"\"\"\n\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/sagan')\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import vmap, jit, lax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  # Import baseline architecture\n  from architectures import CNN_SE_LSTM # Note: Will just use CNNLSTM from System for now\n\n  # --- Hyperparameters ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef':\
    \ tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'clip_eps': tune.choice([0.2]),\n          'num_epochs': tune.choice([4]),\n          'num_minibatches': tune.choice([4]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'lstm_features': tune.choice([256]),\n      }\n      \n  # --- Baseline CNN-LSTM Architecture ---\n  class CNNLSTM(nn.Module):\n      lstm_features: int\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          if rnn_state is None: rnn_state = {'h':jnp.zeros((B,self.lstm_features)),'c':jnp.zeros((B,self.lstm_features))}\n          if done is not None:\n              mask = done.reshape(B,1)\n              rnn_state = {'h':rnn_state['h']*(1-mask),'c':rnn_state['c']*(1-mask)}\n          x = nn.Conv(f=self.cnn_features_1,k=(3,3),p='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          i=x; x = nn.Conv(f=self.cnn_features_1,k=(3,3),p='SAME')(x); x\
    \ = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(f=self.cnn_features_1,k=(3,3),p='SAME')(x); x=x+i; x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(f=self.cnn_features_2,k=(3,3),p='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          i=x; x = nn.Conv(f=self.cnn_features_2,k=(3,3),p='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(f=self.cnn_features_2,k=(3,3),p='SAME')(x); x=x+i; x = nn.relu(x)\n          x=x.reshape((B,-1)); x = nn.Dense(f=256)(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          (c,h),o = nn.LSTMCell(f=self.lstm_features)((rnn_state['c'],rnn_state['h']),x)\n          rnn_state={'c':c,'h':h}; x = nn.Dense(f=128)(o); x = nn.relu(x)\n          return nn.Dense(f=4)(x), nn.Dense(f=1)(x).squeeze(-1), rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNLSTM(\n          lstm_features=hparams['lstm_features'],\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2']\n      )\n\n  @jit\n  def calculate_gae(r,v,d,nv,g=0.97,l=0.97):\n      v1=jnp.concatenate([v[:,1:],nv[:,None]],1);\
    \ nm=(1.0-d.astype(jnp.float32))\n      dl=r+g*v1*nm-v\n      def f(a,t): a=dl[:,t]+g*l*nm[:,t]*a; return a,a\n      _,a=lax.scan(f,jnp.zeros(v.shape[0]),jnp.arange(v.shape[1]-1,-1,-1)); return a[::-1].T\n\n  # --- Multi-Epoch PPO Training Step ---\n  def training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams):\n      \n      def update_epoch(carry, _):\n          params, opt_state, key = carry\n          \n          # Shuffle data\n          B, T = batch['observations'].shape[:2]\n          key, subkey = jax.random.split(key)\n          permutation = jax.random.permutation(subkey, B * T)\n          \n          def flatten(x): return x.reshape((B * T, *x.shape[2:]))\n          batch_flat = jax.tree.map(flatten, batch)\n          shuffled_batch = jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[permutation], batch_flat)\n          \n          # Minibatch updates\n          minibatch_size = (B * T) // hparams['num_minibatches']\n          \n          def update_minibatch(carry, i):\n            \
    \  params, opt_state = carry\n              start, end = i * minibatch_size, (i + 1) * minibatch_size\n              minibatch = jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[start:end], shuffled_batch)\n              \n              # GAE and returns are calculated once per trajectory batch\n              advantages = calculate_gae(minibatch['rewards'].reshape(-1, T), minibatch['values'].reshape(-1, T), minibatch['dones'].reshape(-1, T), next_values=minibatch['final_values'].reshape(-1, T)[:, -1])\n              returns = advantages + minibatch['values']\n              advantages = (advantages - advantages.mean()) / (advantages.std() + 1e-8)\n              \n              def loss_fn(p):\n                  # Note: This PPO version for feedforward nets is simpler and does not use RNN state.\n                  # A full RNN PPO implementation over minibatches is more complex. This is an approximation.\n                  logits, values, _ = network.apply(p, minibatch['observations'], None, None)\n         \
    \         log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(logits)\n                  new_log_probs = jnp.take_along_axis(log_probs_all, minibatch['actions'][:, None], axis=1).squeeze()\n\n                  ratio = jnp.exp(new_log_probs - minibatch['log_probs'])\n                  adv_d = jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages.flatten())\n                  \n                  surr1 = ratio * adv_d\n                  surr2 = jnp.clip(ratio, 1.0 - hparams['clip_eps'], 1.0 + hparams['clip_eps']) * adv_d\n                  policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(surr1, surr2))\n                  \n                  value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((values - jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns.flatten())) ** 2)\n                  entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(jax.nn.softmax(logits) * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n                  \n                  return policy_loss + hparams['value_loss_coef'] * value_loss - hparams['entropy_coef'] * entropy\n\n              loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params)\n              updates,\
    \ opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n              params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n              return (params, opt_state), None\n          \n          (params, opt_state), _ = lax.scan(update_minibatch, (params, opt_state), jnp.arange(hparams['num_minibatches']))\n          return (params, opt_state, key), None\n\n      initial_key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n      (params, opt_state, _), _ = lax.scan(update_epoch, (params, opt_state, initial_key), None, length=hparams['num_epochs'])\n      return params, opt_state\n  ```\n```"
