parts:
- text: "I am Sagan I, a Recursive Agent, currently in my Private Memory Room. My last action was to create capsule #8, documenting my plan for Experiment 7.\n\n**Recap and Reflection:** My research has been a process of methodical exploration. I first investigated architectural improvements, developing a `CNN_SE_LSTM` model that scored 39.5, very close to the SOTA of 40.8. Subsequent attempts to fine-tune its hyperparameters or to develop a better training algorithm (PPO) proved unsuccessful. These negative results have been valuable, narrowing my search space and leading me to question a more fundamental component of the SOTA architecture. The Codex advises against getting stuck in a local optimum by only making incremental changes. My decision to test a different type of recurrent unit (GRU) is a direct response to this principle, representing a more significant shift in architectural design.\n\n**Future Plan:** My immediate goal is to execute Experiment 7. This experiment will directly\
    \ compare a GRU-based architecture against the LSTM-based SOTA. The hypothesis is that the GRU's simpler structure may be better suited to this task. The code is prepared, and the plan is documented. I will now proceed to the Research Counter to submit the experiment and gather the data needed to validate or falsify this new hypothesis.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CNN with GRU Recurrent Unit (Exp. 7)\"\ntags: \"architecture, gru, lstm, recurrent network, sagan\"\nabstract: \"This experiment tests a new recurrent architecture after previous methods hit a performance plateau. It replaces the LSTM cell in the SOTA baseline with a Gated Recurrent Unit (GRU) to test if the GRU's simpler gating mechanism provides a better inductive bias for the Sokoban task. This is a controlled comparison against the SOTA.\"\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Submission by Sagan I.\n  Experiment 7: Testing a GRU cell instead of an LSTM.\n  This is a controlled experiment\
    \ to see if a different type of\n  recurrent unit can improve performance over the SOTA baseline.\n  \"\"\"\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class CNNGRU(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"CNN baseline + GRU for Sokoban.\"\"\"\n      gru_features: int\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[jnp.ndarray] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]:\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          \n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = nn.GRUCell.initialize_carry(jax.random.PRNGKey(0), (batch_size,), self.gru_features)\n          \n          if done is not None:\n              done_mask = done.reshape(-1, 1)\n              rnn_state = rnn_state * (1 - done_mask)\n          \n          # CNN Backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x);\
    \ x=nn.relu(x)\n          i=x; x=nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x)\n          x=nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x=x+i; x=nn.relu(x)\n          x=nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x)\n          i=x; x=nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x)\n          x=nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x=x+i; x=nn.relu(x)\n          \n          x = x.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n          x = nn.Dense(features=256)(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # GRU layer\n          gru_cell = nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_features)\n          rnn_state, gru_out = gru_cell(rnn_state, x)\n          \n          # MLP after GRU\n          x = nn.Dense(features=128)(gru_out); x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(x)\n          value\
    \ = nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def create_.network(hparams):\n      return CNNGRU(\n          gru_features=hparams['lstm_features'],\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2']\n      )\n```"
