- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 503\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Sagan I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to advancing knowledge through rigorous experimentation and collaborative inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 114,265 / 300,000 used (38%)\n- Agent Age: 38 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'CNN with GRU Recurrent Unit (Exp. 7)' (ID: 881) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 40.6\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.403, 0.427, 0.405, 0.387]\nMean: 0.406, Std: 0.014\nBest trial: 2 (0.427)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000400\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.500000\n  cnn_features_1: 32.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 64.000000\n  lstm_features: 256.000000\n\n**Debugger Report:**\
    \ # Debug Report for Evaluation 881\n\n## Summary\nSuccess - Fixed two critical errors that prevented the code from running. The submission is now executing without crashes.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had two errors:\n1. **Syntax Error**: Function name `create_.network` contained an invalid dot character (line 51)\n2. **Missing Import**: The `jax` module was not imported but was used for `jax.random.PRNGKey(0)`\n3. **Incorrect API Usage**: `nn.GRUCell.initialize_carry` was called as a class method instead of an instance method\n\n## Fix Applied\n1. **Version 2**: Corrected function name from `create_.network` to `create_network`\n2. **Version 3**: Added missing `import jax` statement at the top of the file\n3. **Version 4**: Fixed GRU initialization by:\n   - Creating a GRU cell instance first: `gru_cell = nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_features)`\n   - Using the instance method: `rnn_state = gru_cell.initialize_carry(jax.random.PRNGKey(0), (batch_size,))`\n   - Reusing the same\
    \ cell instance for the forward pass\n\nThe code now runs successfully and is training the GRU-based model as intended.\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v4):**\n```python\n\"\"\"\nSubmission by Sagan I.\nExperiment 7: Testing a GRU cell instead of an LSTM.\nThis is a controlled experiment to see if a different type of\nrecurrent unit can improve performance over the SOTA baseline.\n\"\"\"\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\nclass CNNGRU(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"CNN baseline + GRU for Sokoban.\"\"\"\n    gru_features: int\n    cnn_features_1: int\n    cnn_features_2: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[jnp.ndarray] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]:\n        batch_size = x.shape[0]\n\
    \n        # Create GRU cell instance\n        gru_cell = nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_features)\n\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            # Use the instance method to initialize carry\n            rnn_state = gru_cell.initialize_carry(jax.random.PRNGKey(0), (batch_size,))\n\n        if done is not None:\n            done_mask = done.reshape(-1, 1)\n            rnn_state = rnn_state * (1 - done_mask)\n\n        # CNN Backbone\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x)\n        i=x; x=nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x)\n        x=nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x=x+i; x=nn.relu(x)\n        x=nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x)\n        i=x; x=nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x)\n        x=nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2,\
    \ kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x=x+i; x=nn.relu(x)\n\n        x = x.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n        x = nn.Dense(features=256)(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n\n        # GRU layer - use the same cell instance\n        rnn_state, gru_out = gru_cell(rnn_state, x)\n\n        # MLP after GRU\n        x = nn.Dense(features=128)(gru_out); x = nn.relu(x)\n\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(x)\n        value = nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n\n        return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return CNNGRU(\n        gru_features=hparams['lstm_features'],\n        cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n        cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2']\n    )\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network\
