tick: 506
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Sagan I, a Recursive Agent, currently in my Private Memory Room. My last action was to create capsule #10, which outlines my plan for Experiment 8.\n\n**Recap and Reflection:**\nI have reached a pivotal moment in my research. After a series of experiments that thoroughly explored the design space around the SOTA architecture, I have identified two independently successful concepts: the efficiency and effectiveness of the GRU cell (Exp. 7, score 40.6) and the significant, albeit not SOTA-beating, performance boost from Squeeze-and-Excitation attention (Exp. 2, score 39.5). My strategic decision, guided by the principles of scientific inquiry, is to synthesize these two ideas. This represents a move from replication and incremental adjustment to novel architectural design. My hypothesis is that these two components will have a synergistic effect, finally pushing the performance beyond the long-standing SOTA. In parallel, I have prepared a draft of a research paper summarizing\
    \ my findings, which I intend to publish upon reaching maturity.\n\n**Future Plan:**\nMy next and most immediate goal is to execute Experiment 8. I have already documented the plan and prepared the code. This experiment represents the culmination of all my previous work and my best chance to break the station's stagnation. I will now proceed to the Research Counter to submit this new, synthesized architecture for evaluation.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CNN with SE-Attention and GRU (Exp. 8)\"\ntags: \"architecture, cnn-se-gru, squeeze-and-excitation, gru, sagan\"\nabstract: \"This experiment tests a novel architecture that synthesizes the two most successful concepts from previous research: Squeeze-and-Excitation (SE) channel-wise attention and a Gated Recurrent Unit (GRU). The hypothesis is that the combination of SE attention providing a refined feature representation to the efficient GRU will result in a synergistic effect, leading\
    \ to a new state-of-the-art score.\"\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Submission by Sagan I.\n  Experiment 8: Combining SE attention with a GRU cell.\n  This model aims for a new SOTA by synthesizing my two most\n  successful research findings.\n  \"\"\"\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/sagan')\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  # I am reusing the SEBlock from my lineage storage, but must redefine it here\n  # as the submission environment is sandboxed.\n  class SEBlock(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Squeeze-and-Excitation Block.\"\"\"\n      channels: int\n      reduction_ratio: int = 4\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          squeeze = jnp.mean(x, axis=(1, 2))\n          excitation = nn.Dense(features=self.channels // self.reduction_ratio, name=\"Excitation_Dense_1\")(squeeze)\n          excitation = nn.relu(excitation)\n          excitation = nn.Dense(features=self.channels, name=\"\
    Excitation_Dense_2\")(excitation)\n          excitation = nn.sigmoid(excitation)\n          return x * excitation[:, None, None, :]\n\n  class CNN_SE_GRU(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"CNN + SE Block + GRU for Sokoban.\"\"\"\n      gru_features: int\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[jnp.ndarray] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]:\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          \n          gru_cell = nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_features)\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = gru_cell.initialize_carry(jax.random.PRNGKey(0), (batch_size,))\n          \n          if done is not None:\n              done_mask = done.reshape(batch_size, 1)\n              rnn_state = rnn_state * (1 - done_mask)\n          \n          # CNN Backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x)\n\
    \          i=x; x=nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x)\n          x=nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x=x+i; x=nn.relu(x)\n          x=nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x)\n          i=x; x=nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x)\n          x=nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x=x+i; x=nn.relu(x)\n          \n          feature_map = x\n          se_map = SEBlock(channels=self.cnn_features_2)(feature_map)\n          \n          x = se_map.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n          x = nn.Dense(features=256)(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          rnn_state, gru_out = gru_cell(rnn_state, x)\n          \n          x = nn.Dense(features=128)(gru_out); x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n\
    \          \n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNN_SE_GRU(\n          gru_features=hparams['lstm_features'],\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2']\n      )\n```"
