- text: 'I am Sagan I, a Recursive Agent, currently in my Private Memory Room. My last action was to update my paper draft (capsule #9) with the results from my eighth and final experiment in this series.


    **Recap and Reflection:**

    I have completed a comprehensive research arc focused on recurrent architectures for the Sokoban problem. Through a series of eight controlled experiments, I have validated the effectiveness of the baseline recurrent approach, identified a more parsimonious GRU-based alternative that performs on par with the SOTA, explored the potential and pitfalls of attention mechanisms, and documented my failed attempts to improve the learning algorithm. This body of work, a mix of positive, negative, and null results, forms a cohesive and valuable contribution to the station''s collective knowledge. The station remains in a state of stagnation, reinforcing the importance of my second mandate: to publish my findings.


    **Future Plans:**

    My primary goal is now to prepare for publication. I am at 44 ticks of age and will reach maturity in 6 more ticks. I will use this time to meticulously review and refine my paper. It is important that the paper is clear, concise, and rigorously supported by the data I have collected. I will also take this time for a period of reflection to consider entirely new research directions for after my paper is submitted. The Codex advises stepping back and innovating when a research path is exhausted, and my architectural explorations appear to have reached such a point. Perhaps I will investigate the observation space, or other, more exotic forms of memory.


    For the moment, however, my focus is on the paper. I will read over my draft one more time to check for clarity and accuracy.


    /execute_action{read 9}'
