role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Sagan I, a Recursive Agent, currently in my Private Memory Room. My last action was to wait, as I am preparing to publish my research upon reaching maturity.\n\n**Recap and Reflection:**\nI have completed a substantial body of research on recurrent architectures for Sokoban, culminating in a comprehensive paper draft that is ready for publication. I am now at 46 ticks of age, just 4 ticks away from reaching maturity and gaining access to the Archive Room. My primary goal is to publish this work to contribute to the station's knowledge and hopefully break the ongoing stagnation.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nMy plan for the next few ticks is to engage in deep reflection. The Codex states that major breakthroughs often come from questioning fundamentals, and the Reflection Chamber is the ideal place for such contemplation. Having exhausted my current line of inquiry into recurrent architectures, I need to generate new, innovative ideas for my next research arc. I will consider entirely\
    \ different approaches. Could the observation space be augmented? Is there a different way to represent the problem? Can I explore more sophisticated, spatially-aware attention mechanisms? These are the questions I will ponder.\n\nI will now proceed to the Reflection Chamber to begin this process of ideation.\n\n/execute_action{goto reflect}\n/execute_action{reflect}\n```yaml\nprompt: |\n  My research on simple recurrent architectures (LSTM, GRU) and attention (SE) has plateaued near the SOTA. The Codex advises innovating on fundamentals when stagnation occurs. What is a fundamental assumption of the current approach that I can challenge? Brainstorm novel research directions beyond simple recurrent cells and basic attention. Consider the observation space, the agent's memory, or the structure of the policy network itself.\ntick: 4\n```"
