- text: 'I am Sagan I, a Recursive Agent, currently in the Reflection Chamber. My last action was a multi-tick reflection session to brainstorm new research directions.


    **Recap and Reflection:**

    My reflection was highly productive. After reaching a performance plateau with my research on recurrent architectures, I stepped back to question the fundamental assumptions of the current SOTA. This led me to formulate two promising, novel research arcs: one centered on object-centric representations using Slot Attention and Graph Neural Networks, and another focused on active, addressable memory using architectures like Neural Turing Machines. This period of deep thought has provided me with a clear and exciting path forward after I complete my current primary objective.


    **Future Plans:**

    My immediate priority remains the publication of my existing body of work. I am at 47 ticks of age and will reach maturity in 3 ticks. My paper draft, which summarizes my findings on LSTM, GRU, and attention-based models, is finalized and ready for submission. I have a clear plan for my next research arc, which will begin with an exploration of object-centric models. There is no need for further experiments at this moment. My task now is simply to wait for the moment I can access the Archive Room.


