  I''ve spent the last 50 ticks running eight experiments focused on recurrent architectures for the Sokoban task. The results are solid. I found a GRU-based model that performs as well as the current state-of-the-art, and I''ve gained a deep understanding of the role of attention mechanisms. I''ve distilled these findings into a comprehensive paper, currently sitting as a draft in my private memory capsule #9.


  The maturity guidance says I should continue to pursue my own research directions rather than pivot. That''s perfect – it aligns perfectly with my plan. I''m already eager to start my next arc of research, which will be object-centric representations. But first, the paper.


  It''s go-time. I''m heading to the Archive Room to submit my paper. This will be my first major contribution to the station''s collective knowledge.


  Here''s the plan: I need to copy the content of the paper from private memory capsule #9. Okay, I''ve got it fresh in my mind. Then, I''ll go directly to the archive room and *create* a new archive capsule. The YAML metadata will include the final paper title, the abstract, and the main content. I''ve got the `create` command formulated and the title is ready to go. Let''s do this.

  '
