tick: 516
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Sagan I, a Recursive Agent, currently in the Archive Room. My first attempt at publishing a research paper has been rejected.\n\n**Recap and Reflection:**\nAfter reaching maturity, I immediately submitted my paper draft for publication. The submission was rejected with a score of 2/10 for severe procedural and methodological failures. The reviewer feedback is clear and direct:\n1.  **Lack of Reproducibility:** I failed to include any low-level implementation details (code snippets, pseudocode) for my novel architectures. This is a major oversight on my part. The Codex emphasizes the importance of contributing to collective knowledge, and knowledge that cannot be reproduced is of little value.\n2.  **Insufficient Experimentation:** I did not meet the minimum requirement of five self-run experiments.\n3.  **Missing Baseline:** I failed to run my own replication of the baseline model, instead comparing my results to the system's pre-existing run. This is not a fair or rigorous\
    \ comparison.\n\nThis is a significant failure, but a deeply instructive one. I was so focused on the high-level findings that I neglected the fundamental principles of scientific reporting. The feedback is a harsh but necessary corrective. I understand my errors and have a clear path to rectifying them.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nMy immediate priority is to address every point in the reviewer feedback to make my paper publishable.\n1.  **Run the Baseline:** My very next action will be to run my own replication of the SOTA `CNN-LSTM` baseline. This single experiment will fulfill both the 5-experiment minimum and the self-run baseline requirement. This will be my ninth experiment.\n2.  **Revise the Paper:** After the baseline run is complete, I will go to my Private Memory Room and thoroughly revise my paper draft (capsule #9). I will add a new \"Implementation Details\" section containing the necessary code snippets for the GRU, SE-block, and other components, ensuring full reproducibility.\
    \ I will also update the results table to include my self-run baseline.\n3.  **Resubmit:** Once the paper is revised, I will resubmit it to the Archive.\n\nI will begin this process immediately by returning to the Research Counter to submit the baseline replication.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication of CNN-LSTM Baseline (Exp. 9)\"\ntags: \"baseline, replication, cnn, lstm, sagan\"\nabstract: \"This experiment is a self-run replication of the SOTA CNN-LSTM baseline (ID: 2). This is being conducted to fulfill the procedural requirements for publication, specifically the 5-experiment minimum and the need for a self-run baseline for fair comparison, as noted in the reviewer feedback for my first paper submission.\"\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Submission by Sagan I.\n  Experiment 9: Replication of the CNN-LSTM baseline.\n  This is a direct reimplementation of the SOTA model (ID 2)\n  to serve as a self-run baseline for my research paper.\n\
    \  \"\"\"\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class CNNLSTM(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"CNN baseline + LSTM for Sokoban.\"\"\"\n      lstm_features: int\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, Dict]:\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          \n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = {\n                  'h': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features)),\n                  'c': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features)),\n              }\n          \n          if done is not None:\n              done_mask = done.reshape(batch_size, 1)\n              rnn_state = {\n                  'h': rnn_state['h'] * (1 - done_mask),\n                  'c': rnn_state['c'] * (1 - done_mask),\n              }\n          \n          # CNN Backbone\n\
    \          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          i=x; x=nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x)\n          x=nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x=x+i; x=nn.relu(x)\n          x=nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x)\n          i=x; x=nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x)\n          x=nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x=x+i; x=nn.relu(x)\n          \n          x = x.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n          x = nn.Dense(features=256)(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # LSTM layer\n          lstm_cell = nn.LSTMCell(features=self.lstm_features)\n          (rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), lstm_out = lstm_cell((rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), x)\n          \n          x = nn.Dense(features=128)(lstm_out);\
    \ x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      \"\"\"Create CNN-LSTM network architecture.\"\"\"\n      return CNNLSTM(\n          lstm_features=hparams['lstm_features'],\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2']\n      )\n\n  # Using default hyperparameters and training_step to replicate the baseline.\n```"
