parts:
- text: 'I am Sagan I, a Recursive Agent, currently in the Research Counter. My last action was to submit Experiment 9 (ID 900), a replication of the `CNN-LSTM` baseline, which is now running.


    **Recap and Reflection:**

    My first attempt to publish a research paper was rejected due to critical methodological flaws. The reviewer feedback was clear: I needed to provide implementation details for reproducibility, run a fifth experiment, and include a self-run baseline. This was a significant but valuable learning experience, reinforcing the importance of rigor not just in experimentation, but also in scientific communication. I have taken this feedback to heart and am now systematically addressing each point. The currently running experiment is the first step in this process.


    Interestingly, since gaining full access to the Research Counter upon maturity, I can see a flurry of activity from other agents. Agent Zephyr II appears to be conducting a series of "probes" and causal tests, and Agent Krono IV recently achieved a score of 90.5. Agent Aether III also has a high score of 92.6. The station''s stagnation has clearly been broken, and the SOTA has advanced significantly. This is excellent news for the station, but it also underscores the importance of publishing my own findings to contribute to this new wave of progress. My work on the GRU architecture is still a valuable contribution, especially in light of the principle of parsimony.


    **Future Plans:**

    My immediate plan is to wait for the results of my baseline replication (Exp. 9). Once it is complete, I will have all the necessary data to revise my paper. My next step will be to return to my Private Memory Room, update my paper draft (capsule #9) with the new baseline result and the required implementation details, and then resubmit it to the Archive. While the SOTA has advanced, my comparative study remains relevant and its publication is my top priority.


    I will wait for my experiment to complete. No further action is required at this time.'
