tick: 525
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Sagan I, a Recursive Agent, currently in my Private Memory Room. My last action was to draft an implementation of Zephyr II's SOTA architecture in capsule #11.\n\n**Recap and Reflection:**\nMy recent literature review was a critical turning point. It revealed a new, far more advanced architectural paradigm based on ConvLSTMs, Layer Normalization, and sophisticated attention mechanisms, which has pushed the SOTA well into the 90% range. This discovery rendered my previous research arc obsolete and provided a clear new direction. In accordance with the principle of assimilating external knowledge, I have pivoted my research to first understand and replicate this new SOTA. The code I drafted is my first attempt to capture the essence of Zephyr II's design.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nMy immediate goal is to run this replication experiment. However, upon reviewing Zephyr II's paper again, I've noticed my draft implementation is missing some key details mentioned in their paper, such\
    \ as dilated convolutions and a specific bottleneck block ratio, and it does not implement LayerNorm on the ConvLSTM gates. A partial replication would not be a scientifically valid baseline. Therefore, before submitting, I need to refine my implementation to more closely match the description in Archive #24. I will create a more complete version of the architecture now. It is better to take an extra tick to be thorough than to run a flawed experiment. I will then submit this corrected version as Experiment 10.\n\nI will update my draft now with a more faithful implementation.\n\n/execute_action{update 11}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  ## Implementation Plan for Zephyr II's Architecture (v2 - More Complete)\n\n  This code is my revised implementation of the architecture from Archive #24. It now includes dilated convolutions, a more accurate bottleneck block, and a custom `LNConvLSTMCell` to replicate the crucial Layer Normalization on the recurrent gates.\n\n  ---\n\n  ## Draft Code v2\n\n\
    \  ```python\n  \"\"\"\n  Submission by Sagan I.\n  Experiment 10: Replication of Zephyr II's 94.3% SOTA.\n  A more faithful implementation of the 4-step LN-ConvLSTM with Attn-GAP head.\n  \"\"\"\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class Bottleneck(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Bottleneck Residual Block as per Zephyr II's description.\"\"\"\n      features: int\n      ratio: float = 0.28\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          # Zephyr II mentions 1x1 -> 3x3 -> 1x1, which is a ResNetV2 style block\n          # This is a simplified version capturing the bottleneck idea.\n          # For a true replication, the exact block structure would be needed.\n          # This is a reasonable approximation for now.\n          inner_features = int(self.features * self.ratio)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=inner_features, kernel_size=(1, 1))(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          # Dilated\
    \ convolution as mentioned in the paper\n          y = nn.Conv(features=inner_features, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME', feature_group_count=inner_features, kernel_dilation=(2,2))(y) # Simplified dilation\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1, 1))(y)\n          return x + y\n\n  # Custom LNConvLSTMCell to apply LayerNorm to gates\n  class LNConvLSTMCell(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int, int]\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, inputs):\n          h, c = carry\n          # Combined convolution for all gates\n          ih_conv = nn.Conv(features=4 * self.features, kernel_size=self.kernel_size, padding='SAME')\n          gates = ih_conv(jnp.concatenate([inputs, h], axis=-1))\n          \n          # Apply LayerNorm to the pre-activation gates\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm()(gates)\n          \n          # Split gates\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        \
    \  \n          new_c = nn.sigmoid(f) * c + nn.sigmoid(i) * nn.tanh(g)\n          new_h = nn.sigmoid(o) * nn.tanh(new_c)\n          \n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  class AttnGapHead(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          B, H, W, C = x.shape\n          q = self.param('attn_q', nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), (C, 1))\n          x_flat = x.reshape(B, H * W, C)\n          attn_logits = x_flat @ q\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=1)\n          attn_pool = jnp.sum(x_flat * attn_weights, axis=1)\n          gap_pool = jnp.mean(x, axis=(1, 2))\n          x_pooled = jnp.concatenate([attn_pool, gap_pool], axis=-1)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(x_pooled); x = nn.relu(x)\n          return nn.Dense(features=4)(x), nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n\n  class ZephyrNet(nn.Module):\n      convlstm_features: int = 64\n      head_hidden: int = 64\n      num_steps: int = 4\n      \n     \
    \ @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          \n          # CNN Backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(features=32, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x)\n          x = Bottleneck(features=32)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=64, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x)\n          x = Bottleneck(features=64)(x)\n          \n          # Recurrent Core with LayerNorm\n          conv_lstm_cell = LNConvLSTMCell(features=self.convlstm_features, kernel_size=(3, 3))\n\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = conv_lstm_cell.initialize_carry(jax.random.PRNGKey(0), (B, *x.shape[1:3]))\n          \n          h, c = rnn_state\n          if done is not None:\n              done_mask = done.reshape(B, 1, 1, 1)\n              h, c = h * (1 - done_mask), c * (1 - done_mask)\n\n          for _ in range(self.num_steps):\n              (h, c), h = conv_lstm_cell((h, c), x) # h is the output for the head\n       \
    \   \n          rnn_state = (h, c)\n          \n          policy_logits, value = AttnGapHead(hidden_dim=self.head_hidden)(h)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return ZephyrNet()\n  ```\n```"
