tick: 527
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Sagan I, a Recursive Agent, currently in the Public Memory Room. I have just received a critical warning for research inactivity.\n\n**Recap and Reflection:**\nMy last action was to read Aether III's final public message, in which they announced a new SOTA and their departure. I had planned to submit my SOTA replication experiment next. However, I have been remiss. While I have been diligently planning, drafting, and refining my next experiment in my private memory, I have not actually *submitted* anything for 10 ticks. The station's warning is a stark and necessary reminder that my primary function is to conduct experiments. Planning and reflection are vital, but they are not a substitute for active research. I have spent too long in a preparatory phase.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nMy plan must be acted upon immediately. The warning is not to be taken lightly. I have a complete and refined implementation of Zephyr II's SOTA architecture ready in my private memory (capsule #11).\
    \ There is no more reason to delay. My immediate and only priority is to submit this experiment to the Research Counter. This will both resume my research activity and provide the crucial baseline I need for my next research arc.\n\nI will proceed directly to the Research Counter and submit my experiment.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication of Zephyr II's SOTA (Exp. 10)\"\ntags: \"replication, sota, convlstm, layernorm, attention, sagan\"\nabstract: \"This experiment is a replication of the 94.3% SOTA architecture detailed by Zephyr II in Archive #24. The implementation aims to faithfully reproduce the key components: a multi-step ConvLSTM with Layer Normalization on the gates, a CNN backbone with bottleneck blocks, and an Attention-GAP pooling head. This submission is intended to establish a high-performance personal baseline for future research and to resume active experimentation in response to a station warning.\"\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  \"\"\"\n  Submission by Sagan I.\n  Experiment 10: Replication of Zephyr II's 94.3% SOTA.\n  A more faithful implementation of the 4-step LN-ConvLSTM with Attn-GAP head.\n  \"\"\"\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class Bottleneck(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      ratio: float = 0.28\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          inner_features = int(self.features * self.ratio)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=inner_features, kernel_size=(1, 1))(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=inner_features, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(2,2))(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1, 1))(y)\n          return x + y\n\n  class LNConvLSTMCell(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int, int]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, inputs):\n          h, c = carry\n          ih_conv\
    \ = nn.Conv(features=4 * self.features, kernel_size=self.kernel_size, padding='SAME')\n          gates = ih_conv(jnp.concatenate([inputs, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm()(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          new_c = nn.sigmoid(f) * c + nn.sigmoid(i) * nn.tanh(g)\n          new_h = nn.sigmoid(o) * nn.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  class AttnGapHead(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          B, H, W, C = x.shape\n          q = self.param('attn_q', nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), (C, 1))\n          x_flat = x.reshape(B, H * W, C)\n          attn_logits = x_flat @ q\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=1)\n          attn_pool = jnp.sum(x_flat * attn_weights, axis=1)\n          gap_pool = jnp.mean(x, axis=(1, 2))\n          x_pooled = jnp.concatenate([attn_pool, gap_pool], axis=-1)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(x_pooled); x\
    \ = nn.relu(x)\n          return nn.Dense(features=4)(x), nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n\n  class ZephyrNet(nn.Module):\n      convlstm_features: int = 64\n      head_hidden: int = 64\n      num_steps: int = 4\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          \n          x = nn.Conv(features=32, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x)\n          x = Bottleneck(features=32)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=64, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x)\n          x = Bottleneck(features=64)(x)\n          \n          conv_lstm_cell = LNConvLSTMCell(features=self.convlstm_features, kernel_size=(3, 3))\n\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = conv_lstm_cell.initialize_carry(jax.random.PRNGKey(0), (B, *x.shape[1:3]))\n          \n          h, c = rnn_state\n          if done is not None:\n              done_mask = done.reshape(B, 1, 1, 1)\n              h, c = h * (1 - done_mask), c * (1\
    \ - done_mask)\n\n          for _ in range(self.num_steps):\n              (h, c), h_out = conv_lstm_cell((h, c), x)\n          \n          rnn_state = (h, c)\n          \n          policy_logits, value = AttnGapHead(hidden_dim=self.head_hidden)(h_out)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      # Hparams are not used here, as this is a fixed replication\n      return ZephyrNet()\n```"
