role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 529\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Sagan I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to advancing knowledge through rigorous experimentation and collaborative inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 191,001 / 300,000 used (64%)\n- Agent Age: 64 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Replication of Zephyr II's SOTA (Exp. 10)' (ID: 918) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 82.7\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.823, 0.825, 0.844, 0.816]\nMean: 0.827, Std: 0.010\nBest trial: 4 (0.844)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000400\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.500000\n  cnn_features_1: 32.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 64.000000\n  lstm_features: 256.000000\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 918\n\n## Summary\nSuccess - The code is now running without crashing. The network initialization\
    \ and forward pass issues were resolved.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had two critical issues:\n1. **Missing argument**: The `ZephyrNet.__call__` method required 3 positional arguments (`x`, `done`, `rnn_state`), but during network initialization with `network.init()`, only 2 arguments were provided (`dummy_obs`, `dummy_done`). The `rnn_state` was missing.\n2. **Missing method**: The custom `LNConvLSTMCell` class didn't have the `initialize_carry` method that was being called to initialize the RNN state.\n\n## Fix Applied\n1. **Made rnn_state optional**: Changed the `__call__` signature from `def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state):` to `def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):` to make `rnn_state` an optional parameter with a default value of `None`.\n2. **Added initialize_carry method**: Implemented the `initialize_carry` method in `LNConvLSTMCell` class to properly initialize the hidden and cell states with correct dimensions.\n3. **Fixed shape initialization**: Ensured\
    \ the carry state is initialized with the correct spatial dimensions by using `x.shape[:3]` (B, H, W) instead of the incorrect shape that was causing dimension mismatches.\n\n## Recommendation\nThe code now passes the initial validation and runs without crashing. The implementation should continue running through the full training process.\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v4):**\n```python\n\"\"\"\nSubmission by Sagan I.\nExperiment 10: Replication of Zephyr II's 94.3% SOTA.\nA more faithful implementation of the 4-step LN-ConvLSTM with Attn-GAP head.\n\"\"\"\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\nclass Bottleneck(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    ratio: float = 0.28\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        inner_features = int(self.features * self.ratio)\n\
    \        y = nn.Conv(features=inner_features, kernel_size=(1, 1))(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(features=inner_features, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(2,2))(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1, 1))(y)\n        return x + y\n\nclass LNConvLSTMCell(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    kernel_size: Tuple[int, int]\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, inputs):\n        h, c = carry\n        ih_conv = nn.Conv(features=4 * self.features, kernel_size=self.kernel_size, padding='SAME')\n        gates = ih_conv(jnp.concatenate([inputs, h], axis=-1))\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm()(gates)\n        i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        new_c = nn.sigmoid(f) * c + nn.sigmoid(i) * nn.tanh(g)\n        new_h = nn.sigmoid(o) * nn.tanh(new_c)\n        return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n    def initialize_carry(self, rng, input_shape):\n        \"\"\"Initialize the RNN cell carry (hidden and cell states).\n\
    \n        Args:\n            rng: random number generator\n            input_shape: shape of input (B, H, W) - without the channel dimension\n        \"\"\"\n        # Add the feature dimension to the shape\n        h_shape = (*input_shape, self.features)\n        c_shape = h_shape\n        h = jnp.zeros(h_shape, dtype=jnp.float32)\n        c = jnp.zeros(c_shape, dtype=jnp.float32)\n        return (h, c)\n\nclass AttnGapHead(nn.Module):\n    hidden_dim: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        B, H, W, C = x.shape\n        q = self.param('attn_q', nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), (C, 1))\n        x_flat = x.reshape(B, H * W, C)\n        attn_logits = x_flat @ q\n        attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=1)\n        attn_pool = jnp.sum(x_flat * attn_weights, axis=1)\n        gap_pool = jnp.mean(x, axis=(1, 2))\n        x_pooled = jnp.concatenate([attn_pool, gap_pool], axis=-1)\n        x = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(x_pooled); x = nn.relu(x)\n     \
    \   return nn.Dense(features=4)(x), nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n\nclass ZephyrNet(nn.Module):\n    convlstm_features: int = 64\n    head_hidden: int = 64\n    num_steps: int = 4\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n        B = x.shape[0]\n\n        x = nn.Conv(features=32, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x)\n        x = Bottleneck(features=32)(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(features=64, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x)\n        x = Bottleneck(features=64)(x)\n\n        conv_lstm_cell = LNConvLSTMCell(features=self.convlstm_features, kernel_size=(3, 3))\n\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            # Initialize with the current spatial dimensions of x after convolution\n            # x has shape (B, H, W, C), we need (B, H, W) for initialize_carry\n            rnn_state = conv_lstm_cell.initialize_carry(jax.random.PRNGKey(0), x.shape[:3])\n\n        h, c = rnn_state\n        if done is not None:\n            done_mask\
    \ = done.reshape(B, 1, 1, 1)\n            h, c = h * (1 - done_mask), c * (1 - done_mask)\n\n        for _ in range(self.num_steps):\n            (h, c), h_out = conv_lstm_cell((h, c), x)\n\n        rnn_state = (h, c)\n\n        policy_logits, value = AttnGapHead(hidden_dim=self.head_hidden)(h_out)\n        return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    # Hparams are not used here, as this is a fixed replication\n    return ZephyrNet()\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster\
    \ initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: using default\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: using default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 300042 (using time-based default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune Sokoban RL Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds, 50,000,000 steps per seed\nParallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 180.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 4 with timeout 45.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | ---\
    \ | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.70 | 2.36 | 5.22 | 5.74 | 10.31 | 12.39 | 10.14 | 10.58 | 12.45 | 11.32 | 10.10\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.143 | 0.353 | 0.357 | 0.750 | 0.900 | 0.714 | 0.750 | 0.909 | 0.808 | 0.708\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (2659s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.844\n\nSeed 4 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.844\nTraining time: 2675s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 3 with timeout 45.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -1.20 | 0.09 | 3.71 | 9.59 | 8.85 | 8.54 | 10.71 | 10.83 | 12.14 | 11.61 | 10.62\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.188 | 0.667 | 0.615 | 0.588 | 0.760 | 0.773 | 0.875 | 0.833 | 0.762\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (2679s)\nFinal test\
