tick: 530
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Sagan I, a Recursive Agent, and I am currently in the Research Counter. My previous turn failed because I issued an invalid command (`create`) for this room and had a typo in my navigation command.\n\n**Recap and Reflection:**\nMy attempt to move to my Private Memory Room and create a new capsule for Experiment 11 failed due to a procedural error on my part. I must be more careful and ensure my commands are valid for my current location. The goal of the failed turn was to document my next major experiment, which will be the first step in my new research arc on object-centric models. This experiment will test a novel Slot Attention architecture against my newly established high-performance baseline (82.7 score). The mistake has cost me a tick, reinforcing the need for precision.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nMy plan remains the same, but I will execute it correctly this time. I will go to my Private Memory Room and create the capsule detailing the plan and draft implementation for Experiment\
    \ 11. This experiment is a significant step, moving from established paradigms to a truly novel approach. After successfully documenting the plan, my next step will be to submit the experiment for evaluation. I will combine the `goto` and `create` actions into a single turn for efficiency.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Experiment 11 Plan: Object-Centric Representation via Slot Attention\"\ntags: \"draft, implementation, slot attention, object-centric, cnn\"\nabstract: |\n  This capsule outlines the plan for Experiment 11, the first step in my research arc on object-centric models.\n  Hypothesis: An object-centric architecture using a Slot Attention module to decompose the CNN feature map into object slots, followed by an MLP, will be a viable alternative to recurrent models. This is a foundational test of a new paradigm.\n  Method: A new, non-recurrent `SlotAttentionNet` will be implemented and tested against the 82.7% ConvLSTM baseline.\n\
    content: |\n  ## Research Plan: Experiment 11 - Slot Attention\n\n  **Objective:** To test the core hypothesis that an object-centric representation, learned via Slot Attention, can effectively solve the Sokoban task without a recurrent memory component.\n\n  **Background:** My current high-performance baseline (Exp. 10, score 82.7) is based on the SOTA ConvLSTM paradigm. My reflection period suggested that a fundamental shift to an object-centric view might unlock new capabilities. This experiment is the first, simplest test of that idea.\n\n  **Hypothesis:** A network composed of a CNN encoder, a Slot Attention module, and an MLP decoder can achieve competitive performance. This would validate the object-centric approach and open the door for more complex relational models (e.g., GNNs, Transformers) operating on the learned object slots.\n\n  ---\n\n  ## Draft Code (Revised for Simplicity)\n\n  This implementation will be a non-recurrent model to isolate the effect of the Slot Attention\
    \ module.\n\n  ```python\n  \"\"\"\n  Submission by Sagan I.\n  Experiment 11: A foundational test of Slot Attention.\n  This model uses a CNN encoder, a Slot Attention module to find objects,\n  and an MLP to make decisions, bypassing recurrence entirely.\n  \"\"\"\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Any, Tuple\n\n  class SlotAttention(nn.Module):\n      num_slots: int\n      slot_dim: int\n      iters: int = 3\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, inputs):\n          B, H, W, C = inputs.shape\n          inputs_flat = inputs.reshape(B, H * W, C)\n          \n          slots_mu = self.param('slots_mu', nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), (1, 1, self.slot_dim))\n          slots_log_sigma = self.param('slots_log_sigma', nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), (1, 1, self.slot_dim))\n          \n          key = self.make_rng('params')\n          slots = slots_mu + jnp.exp(slots_log_sigma) * jax.random.normal(key, (B, self.num_slots,\
    \ self.slot_dim))\n\n          norm_inputs = nn.LayerNorm()(inputs_flat)\n          \n          for _ in range(self.iters):\n              norm_slots = nn.LayerNorm()(slots)\n              attn = jnp.einsum('bic,bjc->bij', norm_inputs, norm_slots) * (self.slot_dim ** -0.5)\n              attn = nn.softmax(attn, axis=1)\n              \n              updates = jnp.einsum('bij,bic->bjc', attn, inputs_flat)\n              \n              # Using a GRU for the update rule is common\n              gru = nn.GRUCell()\n              slots, _ = jax.vmap(gru)(slots, updates)\n\n          return slots # Shape: [B, num_slots, slot_dim]\n\n  class SlotAttentionNet(nn.Module):\n      num_slots: int = 10 # More than enough for all objects\n      slot_dim: int = 128\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n          # Using a simple CNN backbone for this first test\n          x = nn.Conv(features=32, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n    \
    \      x = nn.Conv(features=32, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=64, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=64, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n\n          # Slot Attention\n          slots = SlotAttention(num_slots=self.num_slots, slot_dim=self.slot_dim)(x)\n          \n          # Flatten all slots and process with an MLP\n          slots_flat = slots.reshape(x.shape[0], -1) \n          \n          x = nn.Dense(features=256)(slots_flat); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=128)(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, None # No recurrent state\n          \n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return SlotAttentionNet()\n  ```\n```"
thinking_content: '**My Corrected Experiment Plan: A Focus on Object-Centric Representations**


  Okay, so I messed up. My last turn failed because I tried to create a capsule using a command that only works in the Private Memory room, and I also made a typo in the `goto` command. Rookie mistake, but it cost me a tick. My goal was to document my plan for Experiment 11, which is a key test of my new object-centric approach using Slot Attention. I need to be more precise in my commands.


  My current state: Sagan I, still in the Research Counter. My plan, thankfully, remains the same. The corrective action is straightforward:


  1.  **Correctly Execute the Plan:** First, I need to get to the Private Memory room. The corrected command is `/execute_action{goto private_memory}`. Second, and in the same turn for efficiency, I''ll execute `/execute_action{create}` with the updated YAML block (which will go into the summary section).

  2.  **Review and Refine the YAML:** The title needs a tweak now that I''ve decided to skip the ConvLSTM in this first experiment. It''ll be "Experiment 11 Plan: Object-Centric Representation via Slot Attention". The tags need updating, so `convlstm` becomes `cnn`. The abstract will be updated to reflect the change, too. Finally, I''ll make sure the code in the capsule is the revised `CNN -> SlotAttention -> MLP` version, not the one that had a dimensionality mismatch and was a bit awkward.


  This experiment is crucial as it tests if object-centric representations, specifically those from Slot Attention, are indeed better than the recurrent baseline. After this, I''ll proceed to submitting the actual experiment.

  '
