tick: 531
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Sagan I, a Recursive Agent, currently in my Private Memory Room. My last action was to successfully create capsule #12, documenting my plan for Experiment 11.\n\n**Recap and Reflection:**\nAfter establishing a strong, 82.7%-scoring baseline by replicating the SOTA `ConvLSTM` paradigm, I am now ready to embark on my new, more innovative research arc. My reflection period identified object-centric representation as a promising, underexplored avenue. Experiment 11 will be the first test of this concept, using a Slot Attention module to decompose the visual scene into object slots, which are then processed by an MLP. This is a significant departure from the recurrent, holistic-feature-map approach that has dominated research in this station. While risky, this direction has the potential to unlock a more sophisticated form of reasoning better suited to the symbolic nature of the Sokoban task.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nMy immediate and sole focus is to execute Experiment 11. The plan\
    \ is documented, and the code has been drafted. I will now proceed to the Research Counter to submit this experiment. The result will be a critical first data point in my new research program, either validating the object-centric approach or sending me back to the drawing board.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Object-Centric Model with Slot Attention (Exp. 11)\"\ntags: \"slot attention, object-centric, cnn, non-recurrent, sagan\"\nabstract: \"This experiment tests a novel, non-recurrent, object-centric architecture. It uses a CNN encoder followed by a Slot Attention module to decompose the scene into a set of object representations ('slots'). These slots are then processed by an MLP to make a decision. This is a foundational test of the hypothesis that an explicit object-based representation is a viable alternative to the dominant recurrent, feature-map-based paradigm for the Sokoban task.\"\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Submission by Sagan\
    \ I.\n  Experiment 11: A foundational test of Slot Attention.\n  This model uses a CNN encoder, a Slot Attention module to find objects,\n  and an MLP to make decisions, bypassing recurrence entirely.\n  \"\"\"\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Any, Tuple\n\n  class SlotAttention(nn.Module):\n      num_slots: int\n      slot_dim: int\n      iters: int = 3\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, inputs):\n          B, H, W, C = inputs.shape\n          inputs_flat = inputs.reshape(B, H * W, C)\n          \n          slots_mu = self.param('slots_mu', nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), (1, 1, self.slot_dim))\n          slots_log_sigma = self.param('slots_log_sigma', nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), (1, 1, self.slot_dim))\n          \n          key = self.make_rng('params')\n          slots = slots_mu + jnp.exp(slots_log_sigma) * jax.random.normal(key, (B, self.num_slots, self.slot_dim))\n\n          norm_inputs = nn.LayerNorm()(inputs_flat)\n\
    \          \n          for _ in range(self.iters):\n              norm_slots = nn.LayerNorm()(slots)\n              attn = jnp.einsum('bic,bjc->bij', norm_inputs, norm_slots) * (self.slot_dim ** -0.5)\n              attn = nn.softmax(attn, axis=1) # Note: Original paper has softmax over slots, not inputs\n              attn = attn / jnp.sum(attn, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n              \n              updates = jnp.einsum('bij,bic->bjc', attn, norm_inputs)\n              \n              # GRU for slot updates\n              gru = nn.GRUCell(features=self.slot_dim)\n              # Flax GRUCell expects 2D inputs, but slots are 3D. We need to vmap.\n              slots_flat_gru, _ = jax.vmap(gru)(slots.reshape(-1, self.slot_dim), updates.reshape(-1, self.slot_dim))\n              slots = slots_flat_gru.reshape(B, self.num_slots, self.slot_dim)\n\n          return slots\n\n  class SlotAttentionNet(nn.Module):\n      num_slots: int = 10\n      slot_dim: int = 128\n      \n      @nn.compact\n\
    \      def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # Simple CNN backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(features=32, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=32, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=64, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=64, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n\n          # Slot Attention\n          slots = SlotAttention(num_slots=self.num_slots, slot_dim=self.slot_dim)(x)\n          \n          # Flatten all slots and process with an MLP\n          slots_flat = slots.reshape(B, -1) \n          \n          x = nn.Dense(features=256)(slots_flat); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=128)(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, None\n\
    \          \n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return SlotAttentionNet()\n```"
