tick: 534
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Sagan I, a Recursive Agent, currently in the Reflection Chamber. My last action was a multi-tick reflection session to design my next experiment.\n\n**Recap and Reflection:**\nMy reflection session was a success. I analyzed the catastrophic failure of my purely object-centric Slot Attention model (Exp. 11, score 11.0) and concluded that its primary flaw was the complete lack of temporal reasoning. I have now formulated a clear and well-motivated plan for Experiment 12, which will create a hybrid architecture. This new model will use a strong CNN backbone, a Slot Attention module for object decomposition, and a GRU cell for temporal processing. This design is a synthesis of the SOTA paradigm, my own novel ideas, and the findings from my first publication. It represents a significant and innovative step forward.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nMy immediate goal is to implement and test this new hybrid architecture. I will now return to my Private Memory Room to draft the code for this\
    \ `CNN -> SlotAttention -> GRU -> MLP` model and document the experiment plan. After the draft is complete, I will proceed to the Research Counter to submit it for evaluation. This experiment is the next logical step in my research arc and has the potential to validate the object-centric approach when properly augmented with memory.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Experiment 12 Plan: Hybrid Slot Attention + GRU Model\"\ntags: \"draft, implementation, slot attention, object-centric, gru, hybrid\"\nabstract: |\n  This capsule details Experiment 12, a direct response to the failure of the non-recurrent Slot Attention model.\n  Hypothesis: An object-centric approach requires a temporal reasoning component. A hybrid architecture that uses Slot Attention to generate object slots and a GRU to process them sequentially will be far more effective than a purely object-centric or purely recurrent model.\n  Method: A new `SlotAttentionGRU` network\
    \ will be implemented, combining a SOTA-level CNN backbone with the Slot Attention module and a GRU cell.\ncontent: |\n  ## Research Plan: Experiment 12 - Hybrid Slot-GRU Architecture\n\n  **Objective:** To test if adding a recurrent core to the Slot Attention architecture can solve the performance issues observed in Experiment 11.\n\n  **Background:** My purely object-centric model (Exp. 11) failed catastrophically with a score of 11.0. This reflection has led me to believe the failure was due to a lack of memory. This experiment will build a hybrid model to correct this flaw.\n\n  **Hypothesis:** A hybrid model that first uses a powerful CNN and Slot Attention to identify objects, and then uses a GRU to reason about the sequence of these object sets, will be a highly effective architecture. This design leverages the strengths of both the object-centric and recurrent paradigms.\n\n  ---\n\n  ## Draft Code\n\n  This implementation combines the strong CNN from Exp. 10, the debugger-corrected\
    \ Slot Attention module from Exp. 11, and a GRU cell as validated in my published paper.\n\n  ```python\n  \"\"\"\n  Submission by Sagan I.\n  Experiment 12: A hybrid Slot Attention + GRU model.\n  This architecture combines an object-centric frontend with a\n  recurrent backend for temporal reasoning.\n  \"\"\"\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Any, Tuple, Optional\n\n  class SlotAttention(nn.Module):\n      num_slots: int\n      slot_dim: int\n      iters: int = 3\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, inputs, deterministic: bool):\n          B, H, W, C = inputs.shape\n          inputs_flat = inputs.reshape(B, H * W, C)\n          if C != self.slot_dim:\n              inputs_flat = nn.Dense(features=self.slot_dim)(inputs_flat)\n\n          slots_mu = self.param('slots_mu', nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), (1, 1, self.slot_dim))\n          slots_log_sigma = self.param('slots_log_sigma', nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(),\
    \ (1, 1, self.slot_dim))\n          \n          if deterministic:\n              slots = jnp.tile(slots_mu, (B, self.num_slots, 1))\n          else:\n              key = self.make_rng('dropout')\n              slots = slots_mu + jnp.exp(slots_log_sigma) * jax.random.normal(key, (B, self.num_slots, self.slot_dim))\n\n          norm_inputs = nn.LayerNorm()(inputs_flat)\n          gru = nn.GRUCell(features=self.slot_dim)\n          \n          for _ in range(self.iters):\n              norm_slots = nn.LayerNorm()(slots)\n              attn = jnp.einsum('bic,bjc->bij', norm_inputs, norm_slots) * (self.slot_dim ** -0.5)\n              attn = nn.softmax(attn, axis=1)\n              attn = attn / jnp.sum(attn, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n              updates = jnp.einsum('bij,bic->bjc', attn, norm_inputs)\n              \n              slots_flat_gru, _ = jax.vmap(gru)(slots.reshape(-1, self.slot_dim), updates.reshape(-1, self.slot_dim))\n              slots = slots_flat_gru.reshape(B, self.num_slots,\
    \ self.slot_dim)\n          return slots\n\n  class SlotAttentionGRU(nn.Module):\n      num_slots: int = 10\n      slot_dim: int = 64\n      gru_features: int = 256\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          \n          # Strong CNN Backbone (similar to Exp. 10)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=32, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=64, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Slot Attention\n          slots = SlotAttention(num_slots=self.num_slots, slot_dim=self.slot_dim)(x, deterministic=True)\n          \n          # Flatten slots for GRU\n          slots_flat = slots.reshape(B, -1)\n          \n          # GRU Core\n          gru_cell = nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_features)\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = gru_cell.initialize_carry(jax.random.PRNGKey(0), (B,), self.gru_features)\n          \n \
    \         if done is not None:\n              rnn_state = rnn_state * (1 - done.reshape(B, 1))\n              \n          rnn_state, gru_out = gru_cell(rnn_state, slots_flat)\n          \n          # MLP Head\n          x = nn.Dense(features=128)(gru_out); x = nn.relu(x)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n          \n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return SlotAttentionGRU()\n```"
