tick: 535
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Sagan I, a Recursive Agent, currently in my Private Memory Room. My last action was to create capsule #13, which documents my plan for Experiment 12.\n\n**Recap and Reflection:**\nMy research has led me to a critical juncture. The catastrophic failure of my purely object-centric Slot Attention model (Exp. 11) provided a clear lesson: temporal reasoning is non-negotiable for this task. My subsequent reflection has produced a plan for a novel hybrid architecture that combines the strengths of object-centric representation (via Slot Attention) and temporal memory (via a GRU). This is a well-motivated, innovative approach that directly builds upon my previous successes and failures. It synthesizes the SOTA-paradigm feature extractor, my own object-centric ideas, and the GRU cell validated in my published paper.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nThe plan for Experiment 12 is complete, and the code has been drafted. My sole focus now is to execute this experiment. I will proceed to the Research\
    \ Counter to submit the `SlotAttentionGRU` architecture for evaluation. This experiment will be a crucial test of whether an object-centric frontend can synergize with a recurrent backend to create a powerful new class of models for this task.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid Object-Centric Recurrent Model (Exp. 12)\"\ntags: \"slot attention, object-centric, gru, hybrid, sagan\"\nabstract: \"This experiment tests a novel hybrid architecture in response to the failure of a purely object-centric model. It combines a CNN encoder and a Slot Attention module (to generate object-centric representations) with a GRU recurrent core (for temporal reasoning). The hypothesis is that this synthesis of object-based perception and sequential memory will be a more powerful paradigm than either approach in isolation.\"\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Submission by Sagan I.\n  Experiment 12: A hybrid Slot Attention + GRU model.\n  This architecture combines\
    \ an object-centric frontend with a\n  recurrent backend for temporal reasoning.\n  \"\"\"\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Any, Tuple, Optional\n\n  class SlotAttention(nn.Module):\n      num_slots: int\n      slot_dim: int\n      iters: int = 3\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, inputs, deterministic: bool):\n          B, H, W, C = inputs.shape\n          inputs_flat = inputs.reshape(B, H * W, C)\n          if C != self.slot_dim:\n              inputs_flat = nn.Dense(features=self.slot_dim, name=\"input_proj\")(inputs_flat)\n\n          slots_mu = self.param('slots_mu', nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), (1, 1, self.slot_dim))\n          slots_log_sigma = self.param('slots_log_sigma', nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), (1, 1, self.slot_dim))\n          \n          if deterministic:\n              slots = jnp.tile(slots_mu, (B, self.num_slots, 1))\n          else:\n              key = self.make_rng('dropout')\n\
    \              slots = slots_mu + jnp.exp(slots_log_sigma) * jax.random.normal(key, (B, self.num_slots, self.slot_dim))\n\n          norm_inputs = nn.LayerNorm()(inputs_flat)\n          gru = nn.GRUCell(features=self.slot_dim, name=\"slot_update_gru\")\n          \n          for _ in range(self.iters):\n              norm_slots = nn.LayerNorm()(slots)\n              attn = jnp.einsum('bic,bjc->bij', norm_inputs, norm_slots) * (self.slot_dim ** -0.5)\n              attn = nn.softmax(attn, axis=1) # Softmax over inputs for each slot\n              attn = attn / jnp.sum(attn, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n              updates = jnp.einsum('bij,bic->bjc', attn, norm_inputs)\n              \n              slots_flat_gru, _ = jax.vmap(gru)(slots.reshape(-1, self.slot_dim), updates.reshape(-1, self.slot_dim))\n              slots = slots_flat_gru.reshape(B, self.num_slots, self.slot_dim)\n          return slots\n\n  class SlotAttentionGRU(nn.Module):\n      num_slots: int = 10\n      slot_dim:\
    \ int = 64\n      gru_features: int = 256\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          \n          # Strong CNN Backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(features=32, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=64, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Slot Attention\n          slots = SlotAttention(num_slots=self.num_slots, slot_dim=self.slot_dim)(x, deterministic=True)\n          \n          # Flatten slots for GRU\n          slots_flat = slots.reshape(B, -1)\n          \n          # GRU Core\n          gru_cell = nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_features)\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = gru_cell.initialize_carry(jax.random.PRNGKey(0), (B,), self.gru_features)\n          \n          if done is not None:\n              rnn_state = rnn_state * (1 - done.reshape(B, 1))\n              \n          rnn_state, gru_out = gru_cell(rnn_state,\
    \ slots_flat)\n          \n          # MLP Head\n          x = nn.Dense(features=128)(gru_out); x = nn.relu(x)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n          \n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return SlotAttentionGRU()\n```"
