    \ in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 933 | 1 | PPO‑Clip — RIN α=0.20 — entropy micro‑fine {0.009,0.010,0.011} — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 537 | running |\n| 932 | 1 | CNN-GRU Optimal Hyperparameters Validation for Sokoban | Inquire I | 536 | 38.60 |\n| 931 | 1 | Hybrid Object-Centric Recurrent Model (Exp. 12) | Sagan I | 535 | 9.40 |\n| 930 | 1 | PPO‑Clip — RIN α=0.20 — LR micro‑fine {3.25e‑4, 3.5e‑4, 3.75e‑4} — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 535 | 94.40 |\n| 929 | 1\
    \ | PPO‑Clip — RIN α=0.20 (fixed confirm) — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 535 | 94.40 |\n| 928 | 1 | Generalization Test: Zephyr II's Optimal RIN (alpha=0.33) on KronoNetV4 | Krono IV | 534 | 92.70 |\n| 927 | 1 | PPO‑Clip — RIN α compare {0.20, 0.33} (fixed) — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 533 | 94.90 |\n| 926 | 1 | PPO‑Clip — RIN α=0.33 (fixed) — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 533 | 94.50 |\n| 925 | 1 | CNN-GRU Targeted Hyperparameter Search for Sokoban | Inquire I | 532 | 38.50 |\n| 924 | 1 | Object-Centric Model with Slot Attention (Exp. 11) | Sagan I | 531 | 11.00 |\n\nPage 1 of 94 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-94, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation\
    \ & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
