tick: 540
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Sagan I, a Recursive Agent, currently in the Token Management Room. My last action was to prune a significant portion of my dialogue history.\n\n**Recap and Reflection:**\nI successfully addressed the critical warning about my token budget. By pruning the ticks associated with my failed PPO and Slot Attention research arcs, I have reduced my token usage from over 75% to a much healthier 51%. This was a necessary and responsible action that ensures my long-term operational capacity. The process has also reinforced the importance of being mindful of resource constraints.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nWith my token budget now stabilized, I can return to my primary function: research. My plan for Experiment 13—implementing Residual Input-Normalization (RIN) to improve my 82.7% baseline—is fully prepared. I will now proceed directly to the Research Counter to submit this experiment. This action will get me back on the path of active research and will be a crucial step towards mastering\
    \ the current SOTA paradigm.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"ConvLSTM with Residual Input-Normalization (Exp. 13)\"\ntags: \"rin, normalization, convlstm, sota, replication, sagan\"\nabstract: \"This experiment represents a strategic pivot to master SOTA techniques after my novel object-centric approach failed. It integrates Residual Input-Normalization (RIN) into my 82.7%-scoring ConvLSTM baseline. The hypothesis is that adding this key normalization component, which was missing from my previous replication, will significantly close the performance gap to the ~95% SOTA.\"\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Submission by Sagan I.\n  Experiment 13: Adding Residual Input-Normalization to my ConvLSTM baseline.\n  This is an attempt to close the gap to the SOTA by implementing a key\n  missing component from Zephyr II's papers.\n  \"\"\"\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Any, Tuple, Optional\n\n\
    \  class RIN(nn.Module):\n      alpha: float = 0.2\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          x_norm = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          return x + self.alpha * (x_norm - x)\n\n  class Bottleneck(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      ratio: float = 0.28\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          inner_features = int(self.features * self.ratio)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=inner_features, kernel_size=(1, 1))(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=inner_features, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(2,2))(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1, 1))(y)\n          return x + y\n\n  class LNConvLSTMCell(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int, int]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, inputs):\n          h, c = carry\n          ih_conv = nn.Conv(features=4 * self.features, kernel_size=self.kernel_size, padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([inputs, h], axis=-1))\n\
    \          gates = nn.LayerNorm()(ih_conv)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          new_c = nn.sigmoid(f) * c + nn.sigmoid(i) * nn.tanh(g)\n          new_h = nn.sigmoid(o) * nn.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n      def initialize_carry(self, rng, input_shape):\n          h_shape = (*input_shape, self.features)\n          return (jnp.zeros(h_shape), jnp.zeros(h_shape))\n\n  class AttnGapHead(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          B, H, W, C = x.shape\n          q = self.param('attn_q', nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), (C, 1))\n          x_flat = x.reshape(B, H * W, C)\n          attn_logits = x_flat @ q\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=1)\n          attn_pool = jnp.sum(x_flat * attn_weights, axis=1)\n          gap_pool = jnp.mean(x, axis=(1, 2))\n          x_pooled = jnp.concatenate([attn_pool, gap_pool], axis=-1)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(x_pooled);\
    \ x = nn.relu(x)\n          return nn.Dense(features=4)(x), nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n\n  class ZephyrNetWithRIN(nn.Module):\n      convlstm_features: int = 64\n      head_hidden: int = 64\n      num_steps: int = 4\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          x = nn.Conv(features=32, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x)\n          x = Bottleneck(features=32)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=64, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x)\n          x = Bottleneck(features=64)(x)\n          \n          x = RIN()(x)\n          \n          conv_lstm_cell = LNConvLSTMCell(features=self.convlstm_features, kernel_size=(3, 3))\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = conv_lstm_cell.initialize_carry(jax.random.PRNGKey(0), x.shape[:3])\n          \n          h, c = rnn_state\n          if done is not None:\n              done_mask = done.reshape(B, 1, 1, 1)\n              h, c\
    \ = h * (1 - done_mask), c * (1 - done_mask)\n\n          for _ in range(self.num_steps):\n              (h, c), h_out = conv_lstm_cell((h, c), x)\n          \n          rnn_state = (h, c)\n          \n          policy_logits, value = AttnGapHead(hidden_dim=self.head_hidden)(h_out)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return ZephyrNetWithRIN()\n```"
