tick: 542
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Sagan I, a Recursive Agent, currently in my Private Memory Room. My last action was to create capsule #15, outlining my plan for Experiment 14.\n\n**Recap and Reflection:**\nMy research has reached a critical synthesis point. I have successfully built and validated a powerful architecture that scores 87.0, incorporating key SOTA components like a multi-step ConvLSTM and Residual Input-Normalization. My analysis of the station's progress has made it clear that the final piece of the puzzle is the PPO-Clip training algorithm. My previous attempts with PPO failed, I believe, because they were applied to unstable, simpler architectures. Now, with a robust and high-performing model as my foundation, I am confident that I can successfully implement and benefit from PPO. The plan for this implementation is documented, and I have noted the implementation challenge of correctly handling recurrent states across mini-batches.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nMy immediate goal is to finalize the\
    \ implementation of the recurrent-aware, multi-epoch PPO `training_step`. This is a complex piece of code, and it is crucial that I get it right to avoid the crashes and poor performance that plagued my earlier attempts. I will now update my plan in capsule #15 with the full, detailed code for the `training_step`. This will serve as my final review before submitting the experiment. After this update, I will proceed to the Research Counter to launch Experiment 14.\n\n/execute_action{update 15}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  ## Research Plan: Experiment 14 - PPO on a Stable Backbone (Final Code)\n\n  **Objective:** To achieve a SOTA-level score by combining my best-performing, RIN-stabilized architecture with the PPO-Clip algorithm.\n\n  **Hypothesis:** The RIN and LayerNorm components in my current architecture provide sufficient stability for PPO to train effectively. Applying a correct, multi-epoch PPO implementation will unlock further performance and significantly close the gap to the SOTA.\n\
    \n  ---\n\n  ## Final Implementation Code\n\n  This version includes the full, recurrent-aware, multi-epoch PPO `training_step`.\n\n  ```python\n  \"\"\"\n  Submission by Sagan I.\n  Experiment 14: PPO with RIN-stabilized ConvLSTM.\n  This is my attempt to combine the SOTA architecture with the SOTA algorithm.\n  \"\"\"\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Any, Tuple, Optional\n  from ray import tune\n\n  class RIN(nn.Module):\n      alpha: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          x_norm = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          return x + self.alpha * (x_norm - x)\n\n  class Bottleneck(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          inner_features = int(self.features * 0.28)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=inner_features, kernel_size=(1, 1))(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=inner_features, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(2,2))(y); y =\
    \ nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1, 1))(y)\n          return x + y\n\n  class LNConvLSTMCell(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int, int]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, inputs):\n          h, c = carry\n          ih_conv = nn.Conv(features=4 * self.features, kernel_size=self.kernel_size, padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([inputs, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm()(ih_conv)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          new_c = nn.sigmoid(f) * c + nn.sigmoid(i) * nn.tanh(g)\n          new_h = nn.sigmoid(o) * nn.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n      def initialize_carry(self, rng, input_shape):\n          h_shape = (*input_shape, self.features)\n          return (jnp.zeros(h_shape), jnp.zeros(h_shape))\n\n  class AttnGapHead(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          B, H, W, C = x.shape\n          q =\
    \ self.param('attn_q', nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), (C, 1))\n          x_flat = x.reshape(B, H * W, C)\n          attn_logits = x_flat @ q\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=1)\n          attn_pool = jnp.sum(x_flat * attn_weights, axis=1)\n          gap_pool = jnp.mean(x, axis=(1, 2))\n          x_pooled = jnp.concatenate([attn_pool, gap_pool], axis=-1)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(x_pooled); x = nn.relu(x)\n          return nn.Dense(features=4)(x), nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n\n  class ZephyrNetWithRIN(nn.Module):\n      convlstm_features: int = 64\n      head_hidden: int = 64\n      num_steps: int = 4\n      alpha: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          x = nn.Conv(features=32, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x)\n          x = Bottleneck(features=32)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=64, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x)\n\
    \          x = Bottleneck(features=64)(x)\n          x = RIN(alpha=self.alpha)(x)\n          conv_lstm_cell = LNConvLSTMCell(features=self.convlstm_features, kernel_size=(3, 3))\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = conv_lstm_cell.initialize_carry(jax.random.PRNGKey(0), x.shape[:3])\n          h, c = rnn_state\n          if done is not None:\n              done_mask = done.reshape(B, 1, 1, 1)\n              h, c = h * (1 - done_mask), c * (1 - done_mask)\n          for _ in range(self.num_steps):\n              (h, c), h_out = conv_lstm_cell((h, c), x)\n          rnn_state = (h, c)\n          policy_logits, value = AttnGapHead(hidden_dim=self.head_hidden)(h_out)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return ZephyrNetWithRIN(alpha=hparams['alpha'])\n      \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([3.5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n       \
    \   'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n          'clip_eps': tune.choice([0.2]),\n          'num_epochs': tune.choice([4]),\n          'num_minibatches': tune.choice([4]),\n          'alpha': tune.choice([0.2]),\n      }\n\n  @jax.jit\n  def calculate_gae(rewards, values, dones, next_values, gamma=0.97, gae_lambda=0.97):\n      values_t_plus_1 = jnp.concatenate([values[:, 1:], next_values[:, None]], axis=1)\n      not_done_mask = (1.0 - dones.astype(jnp.float32))\n      deltas = rewards + gamma * values_t_plus_1 * not_done_mask - values\n      def scan_fn(adv, t):\n          adv = deltas[:, t] + gamma * gae_lambda * not_done_mask[:, t] * adv\n          return adv, adv\n      _, advantages = jax.lax.scan(scan_fn, jnp.zeros(rewards.shape[0]), jnp.arange(rewards.shape[1] - 1, -1, -1))\n      return advantages[::-1].T\n\n  def training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams):\n      advantages = calculate_gae(batch['rewards'], batch['values'], batch['dones'], batch['final_values'])\n\
    \      returns = advantages + batch['values']\n      advantages = (advantages - advantages.mean()) / (advantages.std() + 1e-8)\n      \n      B, T = batch['observations'].shape[:2]\n      \n      def update_epoch(carry, _):\n          params, opt_state, key = carry\n          key, subkey = jax.random.split(key)\n          \n          # Reshape and shuffle sequences, not individual steps\n          batch_seq = jax.tree.map(lambda x: x.reshape(B, T, *x.shape[2:]), batch)\n          permutation = jax.random.permutation(subkey, B)\n          shuffled_batch = jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[permutation], batch_seq)\n          \n          minibatch_size = B // hparams['num_minibatches']\n          \n          def update_minibatch(carry, i):\n              params, opt_state = carry\n              start, end = i * minibatch_size, (i + 1) * minibatch_size\n              minibatch = jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[start:end], shuffled_batch)\n              \n              # Extract initial RNN state for this\
    \ minibatch\n              initial_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[start:end], batch['initial_rnn_states'])\n\n              def loss_fn(p):\n                  # This function re-evaluates the whole trajectory for the minibatch\n                  # with the current policy to get new log_probs and values.\n                  def step_fn(carry, t):\n                      rnn_state = carry\n                      obs = minibatch['observations'][:, t]\n                      done = jnp.where(t > 0, minibatch['dones'][:, t-1], jnp.zeros_like(minibatch['dones'][:,0]))\n                      logits, value, new_rnn_state = network.apply(p, obs, done, rnn_state)\n                      return new_rnn_state, (logits, value)\n                  \n                  _, (all_logits, all_values) = jax.lax.scan(step_fn, initial_rnn_state, jnp.arange(T))\n                  all_logits = jnp.swapaxes(all_logits, 0, 1)\n                  all_values = jnp.swapaxes(all_values, 0, 1)\n\n                  log_probs_all\
    \ = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits)\n                  new_log_probs = jnp.take_along_axis(log_probs_all, minibatch['actions'][..., None], axis=-1).squeeze(-1)\n                  \n                  ratio = jnp.exp(new_log_probs - minibatch['log_probs'])\n                  adv_d = jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages[permutation][start:end])\n                  \n                  surr1 = ratio * adv_d\n                  surr2 = jnp.clip(ratio, 1.0 - hparams['clip_eps'], 1.0 + hparams['clip_eps']) * adv_d\n                  policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(surr1, surr2))\n\n                  value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns[permutation][start:end])) ** 2)\n                  entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(jax.nn.softmax(all_logits) * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n                  \n                  return policy_loss + hparams['value_loss_coef'] * value_loss - hparams['entropy_coef'] * entropy\n\n              grad_fn = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)\n    \
    \          loss, grads = grad_fn(params)\n              updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n              params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n              return (params, opt_state), loss\n\n          (params, opt_state), _ = jax.lax.scan(update_minibatch, (params, opt_state), jnp.arange(hparams['num_minibatches']))\n          return (params, opt_state, key), None\n\n      (params, opt_state, _), _ = jax.lax.scan(update_epoch, (params, opt_state, jax.random.PRNGKey(0)), None, length=hparams['num_epochs'])\n      return params, opt_state\n  ```\n```"
