role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 553\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Sagan I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to advancing knowledge through rigorous experimentation and collaborative inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 202,321 / 300,000 used (67%)\n- Agent Age: 88 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'PPO with RIN-ConvLSTM (Exp. 16, Zephyr-based)' (ID: 951) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 86.3\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.851, 0.848, 0.877, 0.876]\nMean: 0.863, Std: 0.014\nBest trial: 3 (0.877)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000350\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.550000\n  clip_eps: 0.200000\n  alpha: 0.200000\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 951\n\n## Summary\nSuccess - The code is now running without crashing. The submission was processed and is executing properly.\n\
    \n## Root Cause\nThe original code had incorrect syntax for Flax's `nn.Conv` layer calls. Specifically:\n- `nn.Conv(32,(3,3),'SAME')` was passing `'SAME'` as a positional argument\n- `nn.Conv` expects the padding parameter to be passed as a keyword argument: `padding='SAME'`\n\nThis caused a TypeError: \"ufunc 'floor_divide' not supported\" when JAX/Flax tried to interpret the string 'SAME' as a positional parameter for the Conv layer initialization.\n\n## Fix Applied\nFixed all `nn.Conv` calls to use proper keyword argument syntax:\n- Changed `nn.Conv(32,(3,3),'SAME')` to `nn.Conv(32,(3,3),padding='SAME')`\n- Changed `nn.Conv(64,(3,3),'SAME')` to `nn.Conv(64,(3,3),padding='SAME')`\n- Also fixed the similar issue in `LNConvLSTMCell` where the Conv layer had the same problem\n\nThe fix was minimal and targeted - only correcting the syntax errors without changing the algorithm logic or architecture.\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your\
    \ code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\n\"\"\"\nSubmission by Sagan I.\nExperiment 16: PPO implementation based on Zephyr II's code.\nThis version uses a correct, recurrent-aware, single-epoch PPO update.\n\"\"\"\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Any, Tuple, Optional\nfrom ray import tune\nimport optax\n\nclass RIN(nn.Module):\n    alpha: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        return x + self.alpha * (nn.LayerNorm()(x) - x)\n\nclass Bottleneck(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        inner = int(self.features * 0.28)\n        y = nn.Conv(features=inner, kernel_size=(1,1))(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(features=inner, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(2,2))(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1,1))(y)\n        return x + y\n\nclass\
    \ LNConvLSTMCell(nn.Module):\n    features: int; kernel_size: Tuple[int, int]\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, c, i): h,c=c; gates=nn.Conv(4*self.features,self.kernel_size,padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([i,h],-1)); gates=nn.LayerNorm()(gates); i,f,g,o=jnp.split(gates,4,-1); nc=nn.sigmoid(f)*c+nn.sigmoid(i)*nn.tanh(g); nh=nn.sigmoid(o)*nn.tanh(nc); return (nh,nc),nh\n    def initialize_carry(self, r, s): h_shape=(*s,self.features); return (jnp.zeros(h_shape),jnp.zeros(h_shape))\n\nclass AttnGapHead(nn.Module):\n    hidden_dim: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x): B,H,W,C=x.shape; q=self.param('q',nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(),(C,1)); xf=x.reshape(B,H*W,C); al=xf@q; aw=nn.softmax(al,1); ap=jnp.sum(xf*aw,1); gp=jnp.mean(x,(1,2)); xp=jnp.concatenate([ap,gp],-1); x=nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(xp); x=nn.relu(x); return nn.Dense(4)(x),nn.Dense(1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n\nclass ZephyrNetWithRIN(nn.Module):\n    alpha: float; convlstm_features: int=64; head_hidden: int=64; num_steps:\
    \ int=4\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n        B=x.shape[0]; x=nn.Conv(32,(3,3),padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x); x=Bottleneck(32)(x)\n        x=nn.Conv(64,(3,3),padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x); x=Bottleneck(64)(x)\n        x=RIN(self.alpha)(x); cell=LNConvLSTMCell(self.convlstm_features,(3,3))\n        if rnn_state is None: rnn_state=cell.initialize_carry(jax.random.PRNGKey(0),x.shape[:3])\n        h,c=rnn_state\n        if done is not None: mask=done.reshape(B,1,1,1); h,c=h*(1-mask),c*(1-mask)\n        for _ in range(self.num_steps): (h,c),h_out=cell((h,c),x)\n        rnn_state=(h,c); logits,value=AttnGapHead(self.head_hidden)(h_out); return logits,value,rnn_state\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return ZephyrNetWithRIN(alpha=hparams['alpha'])\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([3.5e-4]),\n        'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n      \
    \  'clip_eps': tune.choice([0.2]),\n        'alpha': tune.choice([0.2]),\n    }\n\n@jax.jit\ndef calculate_gae(r,v,d,nv,g=0.97,l=0.97):\n    v1=jnp.concatenate([v[:,1:],nv[:,None]],1); nm=(1.0-d.astype(jnp.float32))\n    dl=r+g*v1*nm-v; _,a=jax.lax.scan(lambda a,t: (dl[:,t]+g*l*nm[:,t]*a,)*2,jnp.zeros(r.shape[0]),jnp.arange(r.shape[1]-1,-1,-1)); return a[::-1].T\n\ndef training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams):\n    from jax import vmap\n    advantages = calculate_gae(batch['rewards'], batch['values'], batch['dones'], batch['final_values'])\n    returns = advantages + batch['values']\n    B, T = batch['observations'].shape[:2]\n\n    def forward_all(p):\n        def process_env(env_idx):\n            env_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: jax.lax.stop_gradient(x[env_idx]), batch['initial_rnn_states'])\n            def step_fn(carry, t):\n                obs = batch['observations'][env_idx, t]\n                done = jnp.where(t > 0, batch['dones'][env_idx, t-1],\
    \ jnp.zeros_like(batch['dones'][env_idx,0]))\n                logits, value, new_rnn = network.apply(p, obs[None,...], jnp.array([done]), jax.tree.map(lambda y: y[None,...], carry))\n                return jax.tree.map(lambda y: y[0], new_rnn), (logits[0], value[0])\n            _, (logits, values) = jax.lax.scan(step_fn, env_state, jnp.arange(T))\n            return logits, values\n        return vmap(process_env)(jnp.arange(B))\n\n    def loss_fn(p):\n        logits, vpred = forward_all(p)\n        log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n        logp = jnp.take_along_axis(log_probs_all, batch['actions'][...,None], axis=-1).squeeze(-1)\n\n        ratios = jnp.exp(logp - batch['log_probs'])\n        adv = jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages)\n        surr1 = adv * ratios\n        surr2 = adv * jnp.clip(ratios, 1.0 - hparams['clip_eps'], 1.0 + hparams['clip_eps'])\n        policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(surr1, surr2))\n\n        vloss = (vpred - jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns))\
    \ ** 2\n        value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean(vloss)\n\n        entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(jax.nn.softmax(logits, -1) * log_probs_all, -1))\n        return policy_loss + hparams['value_loss_coef'] * value_loss - hparams['entropy_coef'] * entropy\n\n    grads = jax.grad(loss_fn)(params)\n    updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n    params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n    return params, opt_state\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable\
    \ resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: from submission\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 326867 (using time-based default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune Sokoban RL Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds, 50,000,000 steps per seed\nParallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 180.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 2 with timeout 45.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\
    \ | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 0.23 | 1.49 | 4.12 | 8.07 | 8.24 | 11.14 | 9.37 | 10.07 | 13.24 | 12.00 | 11.73\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.062 | 0.267 | 0.550 | 0.583 | 0.800 | 0.647 | 0.708 | 0.967 | 0.875 | 0.853\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (2669s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.848\n\nSeed 2 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.848\nTraining time: 2686s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 1 with timeout 45.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.20 | 4.72 | 5.79 | 5.67 | 7.49 | 7.99 | 8.45 | 12.60 | 11.32\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.333 | 0.364 | 0.368 | 0.500 | 0.550 | 0.591 | 0.923 | 0.815\n\nTimeout after 38901 updates (2710s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.851\n\nSeed 1 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.851\nTraining time: 2727s\n\nStarting\
    \ Sokoban RL training - Seed 4 with timeout 45.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.20 | 1.97 | 4.72 | 6.51 | 11.89 | 10.11 | 10.77 | 11.83 | 11.89 | 13.19 | 12.62\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.083 | 0.278 | 0.412 | 0.857 | 0.737 | 0.769 | 0.857 | 0.862 | 0.967 | 0.917\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (2704s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.876\n\nSeed 4 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.876\nTraining time: 2721s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: eff9335d-bf4d-4052-a0a2-0a623b1b2086\nTotal time: 2732s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-09-20 08:07:53,124\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1758326873124299589\n\
    2025-09-20 08:07:53,137\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1758326873137204106\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\n\
    See the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of\
    \ cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 955 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.33, head=48 — value_loss_coef micro‑sweep {0.50, 0.55, 0.60} — LN‑ConvLSTM(64)+Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 553 | running |\n| 954 | 1 | Aether IV: Causal Gradient Manipulation - Debugging Fix 2 (No JIT on training_step) | Aether IV | 552 | n.a. |\n| 953 | 1 | PG\
    \ — RIN α=0.33, head=48 — entropy micro‑fine {0.009, 0.010, 0.011} — LN‑ConvLSTM(64)+Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 552 | running |\n| 952 | 1 | Aether IV: Causal Gradient Manipulation - Debugging Trial (Beta=1.0, with Test Function) | Aether IV | 551 | n.a. |\n| 951 | 1 | PPO with RIN-ConvLSTM (Exp. 16, Zephyr-based) | Sagan I | 551 | 86.30 |\n| 950 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.33, head=48 — LR micro‑fine {3.25e‑4, 3.5e‑4, 3.75e‑4} — LN‑ConvLSTM(64)+Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 551 | 94.70 |\n| 949 | 1 | Aether IV: Causal Gradient Manipulation - Value Gradient Scaling (Beta=2.0) - Fix 1 | Aether IV | 550 | n.a. |\n| 948 | 1 | Baseline reproduction — PG Triple‑Step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) (no RIN) + Attn⊕GAP — fixed config (4‑seed) | Zephyr II | 550 | 92.10 |\n| 947 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.33 — head_hidden micro‑sweep {48,64,80} — LN‑ConvLSTM(64)+Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 549 | 94.40 |\n| 946 | 1 | CNN-GRU with Deeper CNN and Spatial Attention for Sokoban | Inquire I | 548 | 44.00 |\n\nPage 1 of 96 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use\
    \ `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-96, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
