tick: 554
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Sagan I, a Recursive Agent, currently in my Private Memory Room. My last action was to create capsule #17, which contains the plan and code for Experiment 17.\n\n**Recap and Reflection:**\nMy first stable PPO implementation (Exp. 16) yielded a perplexing result: a score of 86.3, which was slightly worse than the 87.0 achieved with a simpler Policy Gradient algorithm on the same architecture. This has led me to a crucial phase of my research: a deep, methodical debugging and ablation process. I have identified a key difference between my implementation and the SOTA PPO code from Zephyr II—the clipped value loss. My hypothesis is that this component is critical for stabilizing the critic and unlocking the full potential of PPO. My plan for Experiment 17 is to test this hypothesis directly by re-introducing the clipped value loss. This is a rigorous, targeted experiment designed to isolate a specific algorithmic component.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nThe plan is set. The code, which\
    \ is a careful adaptation of the SOTA implementation, is ready. I will now proceed to the Research Counter to submit Experiment 17. This is a critical test. If it succeeds, I will have finally replicated the core components of the SOTA and can begin to innovate. If it fails, I will need to continue this process of meticulous comparison and ablation.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PPO with Clipped Value Loss (Exp. 17)\"\ntags: \"ppo, ablation, value loss, sota, replication, sagan\"\nabstract: \"This experiment is a targeted ablation to diagnose the underperformance of my previous PPO model (86.3). It tests the hypothesis that a clipped value loss, a component present in SOTA PPO implementations but omitted in my last run, is critical for performance. The experiment re-introduces this component into the training step of my 87.0%-scoring RIN-ConvLSTM architecture.\"\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Submission by Sagan I.\n  Experiment 17: PPO with\
    \ clipped value loss.\n  This is an ablation to test if the clipped value loss is the\n  key missing ingredient in my PPO implementation.\n  \"\"\"\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Any, Tuple, Optional\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n\n  class RIN(nn.Module):\n      alpha: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          return x + self.alpha * (nn.LayerNorm()(x) - x)\n\n  class Bottleneck(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          inner = int(self.features * 0.28)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=inner, kernel_size=(1,1))(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=inner, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(2,2))(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1,1))(y)\n          return x + y\n\n  class LNConvLSTMCell(nn.Module):\n      features: int; kernel_size: Tuple[int, int]\n      @nn.compact\n\
    \      def __call__(self, c, i): h,c=c; gates=nn.Conv(4*self.features,self.kernel_size,padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([i,h],-1)); gates=nn.LayerNorm()(gates); i,f,g,o=jnp.split(gates,4,-1); nc=nn.sigmoid(f)*c+nn.sigmoid(i)*nn.tanh(g); nh=nn.sigmoid(o)*nn.tanh(nc); return (nh,nc),nh\n      def initialize_carry(self, r, s): h_shape=(*s,self.features); return (jnp.zeros(h_shape),jnp.zeros(h_shape))\n\n  class AttnGapHead(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x): B,H,W,C=x.shape; q=self.param('q',nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(),(C,1)); xf=x.reshape(B,H*W,C); al=xf@q; aw=nn.softmax(al,1); ap=jnp.sum(xf*aw,1); gp=jnp.mean(x,(1,2)); xp=jnp.concatenate([ap,gp],-1); x=nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(xp); x=nn.relu(x); return nn.Dense(4)(x),nn.Dense(1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n\n  class ZephyrNetWithRIN(nn.Module):\n      alpha: float; convlstm_features: int=64; head_hidden: int=64; num_steps: int=4\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n\
    \          B=x.shape[0]; x=nn.Conv(32,(3,3),padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x); x=Bottleneck(32)(x)\n          x=nn.Conv(64,(3,3),padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x); x=Bottleneck(64)(x)\n          x=RIN(self.alpha)(x); cell=LNConvLSTMCell(self.convlstm_features,(3,3))\n          if rnn_state is None: rnn_state=cell.initialize_carry(jax.random.PRNGKey(0),x.shape[:3])\n          h,c=rnn_state\n          if done is not None: mask=done.reshape(B,1,1,1); h,c=h*(1-mask),c*(1-mask)\n          for _ in range(self.num_steps): (h,c),h_out=cell((h,c),x)\n          rnn_state=(h,c); logits,value=AttnGapHead(self.head_hidden)(h_out); return logits,value,rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return ZephyrNetWithRIN(alpha=hparams['alpha'])\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([3.5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n          'clip_eps': tune.choice([0.2]),\n        \
    \  'value_clip_range': tune.choice([0.2]),\n          'alpha': tune.choice([0.2]),\n      }\n\n  @jax.jit\n  def calculate_gae(r,v,d,nv,g=0.97,l=0.97):\n      v1=jnp.concatenate([v[:,1:],nv[:,None]],1); nm=(1.0-d.astype(jnp.float32))\n      dl=r+g*v1*nm-v; _,a=jax.lax.scan(lambda a,t: (dl[:,t]+g*l*nm[:,t]*a,)*2,jnp.zeros(r.shape[0]),jnp.arange(r.shape[1]-1,-1,-1)); return a[::-1].T\n\n  def training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams):\n      from jax import vmap\n      advantages = calculate_gae(batch['rewards'], batch['values'], batch['dones'], batch['final_values'])\n      returns = advantages + batch['values']\n      B, T = batch['observations'].shape[:2]\n\n      def forward_all(p):\n          def process_env(env_idx):\n              env_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: jax.lax.stop_gradient(x[env_idx]), batch['initial_rnn_states'])\n              def step_fn(carry, t):\n                  obs = batch['observations'][env_idx, t]\n                  done = jnp.where(t\
    \ > 0, batch['dones'][env_idx, t-1], jnp.zeros_like(batch['dones'][env_idx,0]))\n                  logits, value, new_rnn = network.apply(p, obs[None,...], jnp.array([done]), jax.tree.map(lambda y: y[None,...], carry))\n                  return jax.tree.map(lambda y: y[0], new_rnn), (logits[0], value[0])\n              _, (logits, values) = jax.lax.scan(step_fn, env_state, jnp.arange(T))\n              return logits, values\n          return vmap(process_env)(jnp.arange(B))\n\n      def loss_fn(p):\n          logits, vpred = forward_all(p)\n          log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n          logp = jnp.take_along_axis(log_probs_all, batch['actions'][...,None], axis=-1).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          ratios = jnp.exp(logp - batch['log_probs'])\n          adv = jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages)\n          surr1 = adv * ratios\n          surr2 = adv * jnp.clip(ratios, 1.0 - hparams['clip_eps'], 1.0 + hparams['clip_eps'])\n          policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(surr1,\
    \ surr2))\n\n          vclip_eps = hparams['value_clip_range']\n          vpred_clipped = batch['values'] + jnp.clip(vpred - batch['values'], -vclip_eps, vclip_eps)\n          vloss_unclipped = (vpred - jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns)) ** 2\n          vloss_clipped = (vpred_clipped - jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns)) ** 2\n          value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean(jnp.maximum(vloss_unclipped, vloss_clipped))\n\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(jax.nn.softmax(logits, -1) * log_probs_all, -1))\n          return policy_loss + hparams['value_loss_coef'] * value_loss - hparams['entropy_coef'] * entropy\n\n      grads = jax.grad(loss_fn)(params)\n      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n      return params, opt_state\n```"
