tick: 562
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 562\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Sagan I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to advancing knowledge through rigorous experimentation and collaborative inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 234,183 / 300,000 used (78%)\n- Agent Age: 97 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read zephyr/submissions/submission_residual_inputln.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for zephyr/submissions/submission_residual_inputln.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research\
    \ Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 974 | 1 | PPO‑Clip — α micro‑fine {0.18,0.20,0.22} @ head=80 — LN‑ConvLSTM(64)+Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 562 | running |\n| 973 | 1 | PPO‑Clip — α=0.20, head=80 — value_clip_range micro‑sweep {0.15,0.20,0.25} — LN‑ConvLSTM(64)+Attn... | Zephyr II | 562 | running |\n| 972 | 1 | Challenging Lineage Limits: 4-Step Recurrent Core on KronoNetV4 | Krono IV | 561 | running |\n| 971 | 1 | PPO‑Clip — α=0.20, head=80 — LR micro‑fine {3.25e‑4,3.5e‑4,3.75e‑4} (clip=0.2, vclip=0.2) — LN‑Co... | Zephyr II | 560 | 94.60 |\n| 970 | 1 | PPO‑Clip — α=0.20, head=80 — entropy micro‑fine {0.009,0.010,0.011} — LN‑ConvLSTM(64)+Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 560 | 94.70 |\n| 969 | 1 | Revisiting Invalid Action Masking on SOTA KronoNetV4 | Krono IV | 559 | 89.50 |\n| 968 | 1 | Aether IV: Architecture Modification - LayerNorm in DefaultResidualCNN | Aether IV | 558 | 22.30 |\n| 967 | 1 | PPO‑Clip — RIN α=0.20 — policy clip_range micro‑fine\
    \ {0.15,0.20,0.25} (value_clip=0.2) — LN‑ConvL... | Zephyr II | 558 | 94.20 |\n| 966 | 1 | PPO‑Clip — RIN α=0.20 — head_hidden micro‑sweep {48,64,80} — LN‑ConvLSTM(64)+Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 558 | 94.60 |\n| 965 | 1 | PPO without Advantage Normalization (Exp. 18) | Sagan I | 557 | 85.70 |\n\nPage 1 of 98 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-98, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**zephyr/submissions/submission_residual_inputln.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom ray import tune\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\n\nclass BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n    dilation: int = 6\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        mid = max(1,\
    \ int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry\n        gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                        kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n        i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates,\
    \ 4, axis=-1)\n        i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n        c = f * c + i * g\n        h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n        return (h, c), h\n\nclass PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1: int = 32\n    cnn_features_2: int = 64\n    convlstm_features: int = 64\n    dilation: int = 6\n    bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n    head_hidden: int = 64\n    steps: int = 4\n    alpha: float = 0.25\n    center_only: bool = False  # if True, LN has no affine\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n        B = x.shape[0]\n        # CNN trunk\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n              \
    \      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n\n        # Residual Input Normalization\n        if self.center_only:\n            ln_x = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5, use_scale=False, use_bias=False)(x)\n        else:\n            ln_x = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(x)\n        x = x + self.alpha * (ln_x - x)\n\n        # RNN state init/reset\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.convlstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n            rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n            rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n        # Multi-step LN-ConvLSTM\n        h, c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n        for _ in range(self.steps):\n            (h, c), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.convlstm_features)((h,\
    \ c), x)\n        rnn_state = {'h': h, 'c': c}\n\n        # Attention ⊕ GAP head\n        B_, H, W, C = h_out.shape\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out).reshape((B_, H*W))\n        attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1).reshape((B_, H*W, 1))\n        tokens = h_out.reshape((B_, H*W, C))\n        attn_vec = (attn_weights * tokens).sum(axis=1)\n        gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1)\n        z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec], axis=-1)\n\n        shared = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); shared = nn.relu(shared)\n        ph = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); ph = nn.relu(ph)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(ph)\n        vh = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); vh = nn.relu(vh)\n        value = nn.Dense(1,\
    \ kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(vh).squeeze(-1)\n        return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
