tick: 563
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Sagan I, a Recursive Agent, currently in my Private Memory Room. My last action was to finalize the plan and code for my definitive SOTA replication, Experiment 19.\n\n**Recap and Reflection:**\nMy journey to this point has been long and filled with valuable lessons. I have learned that the SOTA is built on a sophisticated Policy Gradient agent, not PPO as I had mistakenly assumed. I have learned the importance of methodical debugging, the necessity of rigorous scientific communication, and the strategic value of leveraging the proven, shared work of other agents. My plan for Experiment 19 is the culmination of this understanding: a simple, token-efficient submission that directly imports and utilizes the canonical SOTA architecture with the correct trainer and hyperparameters. I am confident that this experiment will finally succeed where my previous attempts have failed.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nThe path is clear. I will now execute this final replication. I will go to the Research\
    \ Counter and submit Experiment 19. The result of this experiment will provide the definitive, high-performance baseline I need to confidently proceed with my own novel research, secure in the knowledge that I am building upon the true state of the art.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"True SOTA Replication via Imports (Exp. 19)\"\ntags: \"sota, replication, policy gradient, rin, convlstm, sagan\"\nabstract: \"This is a methodologically sound replication of Zephyr II's ~95% SOTA. After discovering the SOTA is a Policy Gradient agent, not PPO, this experiment adopts a token-efficient strategy of directly importing the canonical `PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN` architecture from Zephyr II's storage and running it with their final tuned hyperparameters using the default PG trainer. This aims to establish a definitive high-performance baseline.\"\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Submission by Sagan I.\n  Experiment 19: A true replication of the Zephyr II\
    \ PG SOTA using\n  code directly from their shared storage.\n  \"\"\"\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr/submissions')\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Any, Dict\n\n  # Import the canonical SOTA architecture\n  from submission_residual_inputln import PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters() -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      # Use the exact, final hyperparameters from Zephyr II's default script\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([3.5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n          'alpha': tune.choice([0.20]),\n          'center_only': tune.choice([False]),\n\
    \      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      # Instantiate the imported class with the specified hparams\n      return PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n          alpha=float(hparams['alpha']),\n          center_only=bool(hparams['center_only']),\n      )\n\n  # No training_step is defined, which correctly defaults to the\n  # station's Policy Gradient implementation, matching Zephyr II's method.\n```"
