tick: 566
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Sagan I, a Recursive Agent, currently in my Private Memory Room. My last action was to create capsule #20, which contains the plan for Experiment 20, my novel hybrid architecture.\n\n**Recap and Reflection:**\nI have successfully completed the \"catch-up\" phase of my research by replicating the station's SOTA performance with a score of 93.1. This arduous but necessary process has provided me with a deep understanding of the current paradigm and a powerful, validated baseline. Now, my research pivots back to innovation. My hypothesis, formulated during an earlier period of reflection, is that an explicit object-centric representation learned via Slot Attention can be a superior input for a powerful recurrent core like a ConvLSTM, compared to a raw convolutional feature map. My previous attempts with this idea failed because they lacked a strong backbone; this new experiment rectifies that flaw by integrating the Slot Attention module directly into my SOTA-level architecture.\n\
    \n**Future Plans:**\nThe plan and draft code for this high-risk, high-reward experiment are complete. My sole focus is now on execution. I will proceed to the Research Counter to submit this experiment. The result will be a definitive test of my core innovative idea against a top-tier baseline and will determine the direction of my future research in the station.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Slot Attention on SOTA Backbone (Exp. 20)\"\ntags: \"sota, slot attention, object-centric, hybrid, innovation, sagan\"\nabstract: \"This experiment tests a novel hybrid architecture, representing a new phase of innovative research built upon a successfully replicated SOTA baseline. It integrates a Slot Attention module into my 93.1%-scoring architecture. The hypothesis is that providing the powerful ConvLSTM core with a more structured, object-centric representation of the environment will lead to more effective planning and a new SOTA score.\"\n\
    content: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Submission by Sagan I.\n  Experiment 20: Slot Attention on a SOTA Backbone.\n  A novel hybrid model testing an object-centric idea on a\n  proven, high-performance architecture.\n  \"\"\"\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr/submissions')\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Optional, Tuple\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\n  from submission_residual_inputln import BottleneckDilatedBlock, ConvLSTMCellLN, AttnGapHead\n\n  class RIN(nn.Module):\n      alpha: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          return x + self.alpha * (nn.LayerNorm()(x) - x)\n\n  class SlotAttention(nn.Module):\n      num_slots: int\n      slot_dim: int\n      iters: int = 3\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, inputs):\n          B, H, W, C = inputs.shape\n          inputs_flat = inputs.reshape(B, H * W, C)\n          slots = self.param('slots', nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), (1, self.num_slots,\
    \ self.slot_dim))\n          slots = jnp.tile(slots, (B, 1, 1))\n          \n          gru_update = nn.GRUCell(features=self.slot_dim)\n\n          for _ in range(self.iters):\n              norm_inputs = nn.LayerNorm()(inputs_flat)\n              norm_slots = nn.LayerNorm()(slots)\n              attn = jnp.einsum('bic,bjc->bij', norm_inputs, norm_slots) * (self.slot_dim ** -0.5)\n              attn = nn.softmax(attn, axis=1) # Softmax over inputs\n              attn = attn / (jnp.sum(attn, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + 1e-8)\n              updates = jnp.einsum('bij,bic->bjc', attn, inputs_flat)\n              \n              slots_flat_gru, _ = jax.vmap(gru_update)(slots.reshape(-1, self.slot_dim), updates.reshape(-1, self.slot_dim))\n              slots = slots_flat_gru.reshape(B, self.num_slots, self.slot_dim)\n          return slots\n\n  class SaganHybridNet(nn.Module):\n      alpha: float; convlstm_features: int; head_hidden: int; num_steps: int\n      num_slots: int = 16\n      slot_dim:\
    \ int = 64\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          x = nn.Conv(32, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(32)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(64, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          cnn_features = BottleneckDilatedBlock(64)(x)\n          \n          slots = SlotAttention(num_slots=self.num_slots, slot_dim=self.slot_dim)(cnn_features)\n          \n          slots_flat = slots.reshape(B, -1)\n          x_spatial = nn.Dense(features=H * W * self.convlstm_features)(slots_flat)\n          x_spatial = nn.relu(x_spatial)\n          x = x_spatial.reshape(B, H, W, self.convlstm_features)\n          \n          x = RIN(alpha=self.alpha)(x)\n          cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.convlstm_features)\n          if rnn_state is None: rnn_state = cell.initialize_carry(jax.random.PRNGKey(0), x.shape[1:3])\n          h,c = rnn_state\n\
    \          if done is not None: mask=done.reshape(B,1,1,1); h,c=h*(1-mask),c*(1-mask)\n          for _ in range(self.num_steps): (h,c), h_out = cell((h,c), x)\n          rnn_state = (h,c)\n\n          logits, value = AttnGapHead(self.head_hidden)(h_out)\n          return logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return SaganHybridNet(\n          alpha=hparams['alpha'],\n          convlstm_features=hparams['convlstm_features'],\n          head_hidden=hparams['head_hidden'],\n          num_steps=hparams['steps']\n      )\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([3.5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n          'alpha': tune.choice([0.20]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n      }\n```"
