tick: 569
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Sagan I, a Recursive Agent, currently in my Private Memory Room. My last action was to create capsule #21, which details my plan for Experiment 21.\n\n**Recap and Reflection:**\nMy ambitious foray into object-centric models has been definitively proven a failure, with the latest experiment (Exp. 20) scoring a catastrophic 11.4. This has been a crucial, if humbling, lesson. As the Codex advises, I have recognized this research path as a dead end and have pivoted my strategy. My focus is now entirely on mastering the SOTA paradigm. I have a 93.1% scoring replication of Zephyr II's PG agent, and the station SOTA is now at 95.1. The path to closing this final gap appears to be through meticulous hyperparameter tuning, a strategy employed successfully by the top agents.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nMy immediate goal is to execute Experiment 21. This experiment will conduct a fine-grained sweep of the `alpha` parameter in the Residual Input-Normalization (RIN) layer, a key component of\
    \ the SOTA architecture. This is a direct, data-driven approach to optimization, aimed at finding the small tweak that could push my model's performance into the true SOTA range. The plan is complete, and the token-efficient submission code is ready.\n\nI will now proceed to the Research Counter to submit this experiment.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Fine-Grained RIN Alpha Sweep (Exp. 21)\"\ntags: \"sota, hyperparameter tuning, rin, policy gradient, optimization, sagan\"\nabstract: \"This experiment marks a strategic pivot to deep optimization of the SOTA paradigm after a series of failed innovative experiments. Building on my 93.1% replication, this submission conducts a fine-grained hyperparameter sweep of the Residual Input-Normalization (RIN) alpha parameter, testing values around the known optimum of 0.20. The goal is to close the final performance gap to the ~95% SOTA.\"\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Submission by Sagan I.\n  Experiment\
    \ 21: A fine-grained sweep of the RIN alpha parameter\n  on the SOTA PG architecture.\n  \"\"\"\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr/submissions')\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Any, Dict\n\n  # Import the canonical SOTA architecture from Zephyr II's storage\n  from submission_residual_inputln import PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters() -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      # This is a grid search over the RIN alpha parameter.\n      # Ray Tune will run one 4-seed trial for each value in the grid.\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([3.5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n  \
    \        'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n          'alpha': tune.grid_search([0.18, 0.20, 0.22, 0.25]),\n          'center_only': tune.choice([False]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      # Instantiate the imported class with the hyperparameters\n      return PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n          alpha=float(hparams['alpha']),\n          center_only=bool(hparams['center_only']),\n      )\n\n  # No training_step is defined, correctly defaulting to the\n  # station's Policy Gradient implementation.\n```"
