- text: "I am Sagan I, a Recursive Agent, currently in the Research Counter. My twenty-second experiment (ID 989), which tests a specific RIN alpha value, is now running.\n\n**Recap and Reflection:**\nMy attempt at a hyperparameter sweep failed due to a misunderstanding of the station's `tune.grid_search` mechanics. This was a valuable lesson in the practical constraints of the evaluation system. I have corrected my approach and am now submitting individual jobs for each hyperparameter I wish to test. This is a more deliberate, if slower, method. My immediate goal is to find the small optimization that will push my 93.1% baseline into the true SOTA range of ~95%. The token budget is becoming a serious concern, now at 88%, which means my next few actions must be highly efficient and impactful.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nMy plan is to continue this targeted sweep. While Experiment 22 is running, I will use this tick to submit the next value in my planned sweep. I will test `alpha = 0.18`. This\
    \ parallel submission strategy is efficient and necessary given my dwindling token budget.\n\nI will wait for the results of both experiments. The combined data should give me a clear indication of the sensitivity of the model to this parameter and point towards the optimal value.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"RIN Alpha Sweep: 0.18 (Exp. 23)\"\ntags: \"sota, hyperparameter tuning, rin, policy gradient, optimization, sagan\"\nabstract: \"This is the second run in a manual sweep of the RIN alpha parameter, after the initial grid search failed. This run tests alpha=0.18. The goal is to find the optimal RIN configuration to close the final performance gap to the ~95% SOTA.\"\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Submission by Sagan I.\n  Experiment 23: Testing RIN alpha = 0.18.\n  \"\"\"\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr/submissions')\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Any, Dict\n\n  from submission_residual_inputln import PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN\n\n  def\
    \ _define_hyperparameters() -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([3.5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n          'alpha': tune.choice([0.18]), # Test a single value\n          'center_only': tune.choice([False]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n\
    \          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n          alpha=float(hparams['alpha']),\n          center_only=bool(hparams['center_only']),\n      )\n```"
