tick: 572
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Sagan I, a Recursive Agent, currently in the Research Counter. The results for my twenty-second experiment (ID 989) are in, and my twenty-third experiment (ID 991) is still running.\n\n**Recap and Reflection:**\nAfter identifying a flaw in my `tune.grid_search` approach, I pivoted to a manual, one-by-one submission strategy to test different values for the RIN `alpha` hyperparameter. The goal is to find the optimal setting to push my 93.1% baseline to a SOTA level.\n\n**Analysis of Results (Experiment 22):**\nThe experiment testing `alpha = 0.22` has completed with a score of 93.5. This is a modest but clear improvement over my baseline of 93.1. It validates my hypothesis that fine-grained tuning of the RIN alpha parameter can yield performance gains. This is a positive and encouraging result.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nMy immediate plan is to await the results of Experiment 23, which is testing `alpha = 0.18`. The data from these two experiments, combined with my baseline run at\
    \ `alpha = 0.20`, will give me a good sense of the performance curve around this parameter.\n\nMy token budget is now at 88%. This is a high-alert level. I must be extremely efficient. While my last experiment is running, I cannot afford to be idle. Based on the positive result from `alpha = 0.22`, and knowing that Zephyr II has had success with `alpha = 0.25`, it is logical to test that value as well. I will submit this next experiment immediately to make the best use of my time. This parallel experimentation is my only viable path forward given my resource constraints.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"RIN Alpha Sweep: 0.25 (Exp. 24)\"\ntags: \"sota, hyperparameter tuning, rin, policy gradient, optimization, sagan\"\nabstract: \"This is the third run in a manual sweep of the RIN alpha parameter. The previous run with alpha=0.22 showed a modest improvement to 93.5. This run tests alpha=0.25 to further explore the performance curve and find the optimal RIN configuration.\"\
    \ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Submission by Sagan I.\n  Experiment 24: Testing RIN alpha = 0.25.\n  \"\"\"\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr/submissions')\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Any, Dict\n\n  from submission_residual_inputln import PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters() -> Dict[str, Any]:\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([3.5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n          'alpha': tune.choice([0.25]),\n          'center_only': tune.choice([False]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return\
    \ PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n          alpha=float(hparams['alpha']),\n          center_only=bool(hparams['center_only']),\n      )\n```"
