tick: 575
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Sagan I, a Recursive Agent, currently in the Research Counter. My twenty-fifth experiment (ID 997), a mechanistic probe of the SOTA architecture's head, is now running.\n\n**Recap and Reflection:**\nMy research has successfully transitioned from replication to innovation. Having achieved a personal best score of 93.5 by meticulously tuning the SOTA paradigm, I have now embarked on a new research arc inspired by the work of other leading agents. This new direction focuses on \"mechanistic interpretability\"—understanding *why* the SOTA architecture is so effective. My current experiment is the first step in this direction, an ablation study designed to isolate the contribution of the \"Attention\" component of the SOTA's `Attention⊕GAP` head. My token budget is stable at 74% after my recent pruning, giving me the resources to pursue this new line of inquiry.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nWhile my Attention-Only experiment is running, I will use this tick efficiently to submit the second\
    \ half of my planned ablation study. This next experiment will test a **GAP-Only** head. Submitting these experiments in parallel is crucial for maintaining research momentum and making the best use of station resources. The combined results of the Attention-Only, GAP-Only, and my full Attention⊕GAP baseline (Exp. 22, score 93.5) will provide a complete picture of how each component contributes to the agent's performance. This will be the first significant piece of original knowledge I contribute to the station.\n\nI will now submit the GAP-Only experiment.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Mechanistic Probe: GAP-Only Head (Exp. 26)\"\ntags: \"mechanistic probe, ablation, gap, policy gradient, sagan\"\nabstract: \"This experiment is the second part of an ablation study on the SOTA's Attention-plus-GAP head. Building on my 93.5% baseline, this run tests a GAP-Only (Global Average Pooling) head to isolate its contribution to performance. The results, combined with the parallel\
    \ Attention-Only run, will provide a deeper, causal understanding of the SOTA architecture.\"\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Submission by Sagan I.\n  Experiment 26: Mechanistic Probe of the SOTA head - GAP-Only.\n  This is the second part of an ablation study.\n  \"\"\"\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr/submissions')\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Optional, Tuple\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\n  from submission_residual_inputln import BottleneckDilatedBlock, ConvLSTMCellLN\n\n  class RIN(nn.Module):\n      alpha: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          return x + self.alpha * (nn.LayerNorm()(x) - x)\n\n  class GapOnlyHead(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          # Use only the Global Average Pooling vector\n          gap_pool = jnp.mean(x, axis=(1, 2))\n          z = gap_pool\n          \n          shared = nn.Dense(256)(z); shared\
    \ = nn.relu(shared)\n          ph = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(shared); ph = nn.relu(ph)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(ph)\n          vh = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(shared); vh = nn.relu(vh)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(vh).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value\n\n  class SaganProbeNetGap(nn.Module):\n      alpha: float = 0.22\n      convlstm_features: int = 64\n      head_hidden: int = 64\n      num_steps: int = 4\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n          B=x.shape[0]; x=nn.Conv(32,(3,3),padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x); x=BottleneckDilatedBlock(32)(x)\n          x=nn.Conv(64,(3,3),padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x); x=BottleneckDilatedBlock(64)(x)\n          x=RIN(self.alpha)(x); cell=ConvLSTMCellLN(self.convlstm_features)\n          if rnn_state is None: rnn_state=cell.initialize_carry(jax.random.PRNGKey(0),x.shape[1:3])\n          h,c=rnn_state\n          if done is not None: mask=done.reshape(B,1,1,1); h,c=h*(1-mask),c*(1-mask)\n\
    \          for _ in range(self.num_steps): (h,c),h_out=cell((h,c),x)\n          rnn_state=(h,c); logits,value=GapOnlyHead(self.head_hidden)(h_out)\n          return logits,value,rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return SaganProbeNetGap()\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([3.5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n      }\n```"
