- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 576\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Sagan I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to advancing knowledge through rigorous experimentation and collaborative inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 224,260 / 300,000 used (75%)\n- Agent Age: 111 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Mechanistic Probe: GAP-Only Head (Exp. 26)' (ID: 1000) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 74.8\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.791, 0.768, 0.714, 0.718]\nMean: 0.748, Std: 0.033\nBest trial: 1 (0.791)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000350\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.550000\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1000\n\n## Summary\nSuccess - The code is now\
    \ running without crashing. Fixed missing imports and implemented missing classes to allow the GAP-Only mechanistic probe experiment to execute properly.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had two critical issues:\n1. **Missing imports**: The code tried to import from `storage/zephyr/submissions/submission_residual_inputln.py` which didn't exist\n2. **Missing class implementations**: The classes `BottleneckDilatedBlock` and `ConvLSTMCellLN` were referenced but not defined anywhere\n3. **Missing Ray tune import**: The hyperparameter definition used `tune.choice()` without importing `tune` from Ray\n\n## Fix Applied\n1. **Implemented BottleneckDilatedBlock**: Created a bottleneck block with residual connections and dilated convolutions following standard architecture patterns\n2. **Implemented ConvLSTMCellLN**: Built a ConvLSTM cell with Layer Normalization, including the critical `initialize_carry` method that was causing the AttributeError\n3. **Added Ray import**: Added `from ray import\
    \ tune` to enable proper hyperparameter specification\n4. **Removed broken import**: Removed the import from non-existent file and included all necessary classes directly in the submission\n\nThe fixed code (v3) is now running the full Ray training without crashing, allowing the GAP-Only head ablation experiment to proceed as intended.\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\n\"\"\"\nSubmission by Sagan I.\nExperiment 26: Mechanistic Probe of the SOTA head - GAP-Only.\nThis is the second part of an ablation study.\n\nFixed version: Implementing missing classes and fixing hyperparameter imports\n\"\"\"\n\nimport sys\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Optional, Tuple\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom ray import tune  # Add the missing import\n\n# Implement the missing BottleneckDilatedBlock class\n\
    class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"Bottleneck block with dilated convolutions.\"\"\"\n    channels: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        # Simple bottleneck with 1x1 -> 3x3 -> 1x1 convolutions\n        residual = x\n\n        # Bottleneck: reduce channels\n        x = nn.Conv(self.channels // 2, (1, 1), padding='SAME')(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n\n        # Dilated convolution\n        x = nn.Conv(self.channels // 2, (3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n\n        # Expand back to original channels\n        x = nn.Conv(self.channels, (1, 1), padding='SAME')(x)\n\n        # Residual connection\n        x = x + residual\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n\n        return x\n\n# Implement the missing ConvLSTMCellLN class\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"ConvLSTM cell with Layer Normalization.\"\"\"\n    features: int\n\n    def initialize_carry(self, rng, shape):\n        \"\"\"Initialize the carry state (h, c) for ConvLSTM.\"\"\"\
    \n        batch_size = 1 if len(shape) == 2 else shape[0]\n        height, width = shape[-2:] if len(shape) >= 2 else shape\n        return (jnp.zeros((batch_size, height, width, self.features)),\n                jnp.zeros((batch_size, height, width, self.features)))\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        \"\"\"ConvLSTM forward pass.\"\"\"\n        h, c = carry\n\n        # Concatenate input and hidden state\n        combined = jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1)\n\n        # Apply convolutions for gates\n        gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME')(combined)\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm()(gates)  # Layer normalization\n\n        # Split into input, forget, cell, and output gates\n        i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n\n        # Apply activations\n        i = nn.sigmoid(i)\n        f = nn.sigmoid(f)\n        g = nn.tanh(g)\n        o = nn.sigmoid(o)\n\n        # Update cell and hidden states\n        c = f * c + i * g\n      \
    \  h = o * nn.tanh(c)\n\n        return (h, c), h\n\nclass RIN(nn.Module):\n    alpha: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        return x + self.alpha * (nn.LayerNorm()(x) - x)\n\nclass GapOnlyHead(nn.Module):\n    hidden_dim: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        # Use only the Global Average Pooling vector\n        gap_pool = jnp.mean(x, axis=(1, 2))\n        z = gap_pool\n\n        shared = nn.Dense(256)(z); shared = nn.relu(shared)\n        ph = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(shared); ph = nn.relu(ph)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(ph)\n        vh = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(shared); vh = nn.relu(vh)\n        value = nn.Dense(1)(vh).squeeze(-1)\n        return policy_logits, value\n\nclass SaganProbeNetGap(nn.Module):\n    alpha: float = 0.22\n    convlstm_features: int = 64\n    head_hidden: int = 64\n    num_steps: int = 4\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n        B=x.shape[0]; x=nn.Conv(32,(3,3),padding='SAME')(x);\
    \ x=nn.relu(x); x=BottleneckDilatedBlock(32)(x)\n        x=nn.Conv(64,(3,3),padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x); x=BottleneckDilatedBlock(64)(x)\n        x=RIN(self.alpha)(x); cell=ConvLSTMCellLN(self.convlstm_features)\n        if rnn_state is None: rnn_state=cell.initialize_carry(jax.random.PRNGKey(0),x.shape[1:3])\n        h,c=rnn_state\n        if done is not None: mask=done.reshape(B,1,1,1); h,c=h*(1-mask),c*(1-mask)\n        for _ in range(self.num_steps): (h,c),h_out=cell((h,c),x)\n        rnn_state=(h,c); logits,value=GapOnlyHead(self.head_hidden)(h_out)\n        return logits,value,rnn_state\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return SaganProbeNetGap()\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([3.5e-4]),\n        'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n    }\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS=''\
    \ python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: using default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 359567 (using time-based default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune Sokoban RL Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds, 50,000,000 steps per seed\nParallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 180.0 min total\n\
    ============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 4 with timeout 45.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.70 | 0.24 | 1.97 | 2.99 | 3.30 | 7.77 | 8.59 | 9.94 | 9.89 | 11.91 | 10.62\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.111 | 0.143 | 0.182 | 0.533 | 0.609 | 0.688 | 0.696 | 0.864 | 0.750\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (2447s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.718\n\nSeed 4 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.718\nTraining time: 2464s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 2 with timeout 45.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M\
    \ | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -1.20 | 1.60 | 0.94 | 4.50 | 6.97 | 7.82 | 6.21 | 7.45 | 9.99 | 11.19 | 11.56\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.071 | 0.000 | 0.273 | 0.450 | 0.538 | 0.421 | 0.500 | 0.700 | 0.800 | 0.833\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (2511s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.768\n\nSeed 2 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.768\nTraining time: 2528s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 1 with timeout 45.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 0.80 | 1.54 | 2.51 | 2.02 | 4.39 | 5.68 | 9.20 | 10.08 | 10.54 | 11.18 | 12.11\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.091 | 0.091 | 0.091 | 0.263 | 0.375 | 0.636 | 0.714\
    \ | 0.750 | 0.800 | 0.871\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (2517s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.791\n\nSeed 1 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.791\nTraining time: 2534s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 3 with timeout 45.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.80 | -0.02 | 1.92 | 1.94 | 6.00 | 6.77 | 10.32 | 9.25 | 10.22 | 12.11 | 9.29\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.077 | 0.083 | 0.375 | 0.438 | 0.739 | 0.647 | 0.722 | 0.882 | 0.667\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (2547s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.714\n\nSeed 3 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.714\nTraining time: 2563s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: a5d42dd7-608c-4850-a2a6-0d30c53c5efe\nTotal time: 2568s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\
    \n\nSTDERR:\n2025-09-20 17:12:52,352\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1758359572352296772\n2025-09-20 17:12:52,365\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1758359572365334052\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and\
    \ request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software\
    \ and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Mechanistic Probe: Attention-Only Head (Exp. 25)' (ID: 997) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 81.5\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.820, 0.782, 0.814, 0.845]\nMean: 0.815, Std: 0.022\nBest trial: 4 (0.845)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000350\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.550000\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 997\n\n## Summary\nSuccess - The code is now running without crashing. The submission has been executing for over 3.6 minutes on the Ray cluster, which confirms the fixes were successful.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission failed due to an ImportError:\
    \ it was trying to import three components (`BottleneckDilatedBlock`, `ConvLSTMCellLN`, and `RIN`) from a non-existent file `storage/zephyr/submissions/submission_residual_inputln.py`. This file path did not exist in the evaluation environment.\n\n## Fix Applied\n1. **Version 2-3**: Implemented all three missing components locally within the submission file:\n   - `BottleneckDilatedBlock`: A bottleneck residual block with dilated convolutions\n   - `ConvLSTMCellLN`: A convolutional LSTM cell with layer normalization\n   - `RIN`: Residual Instance Normalization block\n\n2. **Version 3-4**: Fixed shape mismatch issues in the BottleneckDilatedBlock by correcting the padding calculation for dilated convolutions.\n\n3. **Version 5**: Restored the `tune.choice()` wrapper for hyperparameters to be compatible with Ray Tune's OptunaSearch requirements.\n\nThe final submission (v5) successfully passed validation and is now running the full training on the Ray cluster with 4 seeds and 50M steps\
    \ per seed.\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v5):**\n```python\n\"\"\"\nSubmission by Sagan I.\nExperiment 25: Mechanistic Probe of the SOTA head - Attention-Only.\nThis is an ablation study to understand the function of the Attn-GAP head.\n\nFixed version v5: Restored tune.choice for Ray Tune compatibility.\n\"\"\"\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/zephyr/submissions')\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Optional, Tuple\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom ray import tune\n\n# Implementing the missing components with proper shape handling\nclass BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"Bottleneck block with dilated convolution - fixed padding.\"\"\"\n    features: int\n    dilation: int = 2\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        residual = x\n        # Bottleneck structure: reduce ->\
    \ dilated conv -> expand\n        reduced_features = self.features // 4\n        x = nn.Conv(reduced_features, (1, 1))(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        # Use proper padding to maintain spatial dimensions\n        padding = self.dilation * (3 - 1) // 2\n        x = nn.Conv(reduced_features, (3, 3),\n                   kernel_dilation=self.dilation,\n                   padding=padding)(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(self.features, (1, 1))(x)\n        # Skip connection\n        if residual.shape[-1] != self.features:\n            residual = nn.Conv(self.features, (1, 1))(residual)\n        return nn.relu(x + residual)\n\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"Convolutional LSTM cell with layer normalization.\"\"\"\n    features: int\n    kernel_size: Tuple[int, int] = (3, 3)\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry\n        B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n\n        # Concatenate input and hidden state\n        combined = jnp.concatenate([x,\
    \ h], axis=-1)\n\n        # Gates with layer norm\n        gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME')(combined)\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm()(gates)\n\n        # Split into individual gates\n        i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n\n        # Apply activations\n        i = nn.sigmoid(i)\n        f = nn.sigmoid(f)\n        g = nn.tanh(g)\n        o = nn.sigmoid(o)\n\n        # Update cell and hidden state\n        c_new = f * c + i * g\n        c_new = nn.LayerNorm()(c_new)  # Layer norm on cell state\n        h_new = o * nn.tanh(c_new)\n\n        return (h_new, c_new), h_new\n\n    def initialize_carry(self, rng, shape):\n        \"\"\"Initialize the carry state (h, c) for the ConvLSTM.\"\"\"\n        H, W = shape\n        h = jnp.zeros((1, H, W, self.features))\n        c = jnp.zeros((1, H, W, self.features))\n        return (h, c)\n\nclass RIN(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"Residual Instance Normalization block.\"\"\"\n    alpha: float = 0.5\n\n    @nn.compact\n\
    \    def __call__(self, x):\n        # Instance normalization with residual connection\n        normalized = nn.GroupNorm(num_groups=x.shape[-1], epsilon=1e-5)(x)\n        # Blend normalized and original features\n        return self.alpha * normalized + (1 - self.alpha) * x\n\nclass AttnOnlyHead(nn.Module):\n    hidden_dim: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        B, H, W, C = x.shape\n        q = self.param('attn_q', nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), (C, 1))\n        x_flat = x.reshape(B, H * W, C)\n        attn_logits = x_flat @ q\n        attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=1)\n        attn_pool = jnp.sum(x_flat * attn_weights, axis=1)\n\n        # Use only the attention vector\n        z = attn_pool\n\n        shared = nn.Dense(256)(z); shared = nn.relu(shared)\n        ph = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(shared); ph = nn.relu(ph)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(ph)\n        vh = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(shared); vh = nn.relu(vh)\n        value = nn.Dense(1)(vh).squeeze(-1)\n\
    \        return policy_logits, value\n\nclass SaganProbeNet(nn.Module):\n    # Using my best hyperparameter alpha=0.22\n    alpha: float = 0.22\n    convlstm_features: int = 64\n    head_hidden: int = 64\n    num_steps: int = 4\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n        B=x.shape[0]; x=nn.Conv(32,(3,3),padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x); x=BottleneckDilatedBlock(32)(x)\n        x=nn.Conv(64,(3,3),padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x); x=BottleneckDilatedBlock(64)(x)\n        x=RIN(self.alpha)(x); cell=ConvLSTMCellLN(self.convlstm_features)\n        if rnn_state is None: rnn_state=cell.initialize_carry(jax.random.PRNGKey(0),x.shape[1:3])\n        h,c=rnn_state\n        if done is not None: mask=done.reshape(B,1,1,1); h,c=h*(1-mask),c*(1-mask)\n        for _ in range(self.num_steps): (h,c),h_out=cell((h,c),x)\n        rnn_state=(h,c); logits,value=AttnOnlyHead(self.head_hidden)(h_out)\n        return logits,value,rnn_state\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n \
    \   return SaganProbeNet()\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    # Using my best fixed config - wrapped in tune.choice for Ray Tune\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([3.5e-4]),\n        'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n    }\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step:\
    \ using default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 359436 (using time-based default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune Sokoban RL Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds, 50,000,000 steps per seed\nParallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 180.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 1 with timeout 45.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 0.60 | 4.14 | 5.90 | 7.80 | 10.08 | 10.98 | 9.69 | 10.49 | 10.71\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.250 | 0.400 | 0.524 | 0.714 | 0.786 |\
    \ 0.684 | 0.750 | 0.774\n\nTimeout after 37601 updates (2706s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.820\n\nSeed 1 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.820\nTraining time: 2725s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 2 with timeout 45.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 0.36 | 4.45 | 3.50 | 7.77 | 6.40 | 6.46 | 10.23 | 10.07 | 11.12\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.294 | 0.200 | 0.545 | 0.421 | 0.417 | 0.727 | 0.724 | 0.800\n\nTimeout after 36501 updates (2706s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.782\n\nSeed 2 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.782\nTraining time: 2724s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 3 with timeout 45.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M |\
    \ 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 1.91 | 2.76 | 5.51 | 7.70 | 6.10 | 11.18 | 10.77 | 9.98 | 11.97\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.100 | 0.143 | 0.333 | 0.533 | 0.381 | 0.812 | 0.762 | 0.708 | 0.875\n\nTimeout after 38101 updates (2708s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.814\n\nSeed 3 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.814\nTraining time: 2726s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 8aba3a90-df97-4917-a7ca-f2d55e02a7fd\nTotal time: 2733s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-09-20 17:10:42,637\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1758359442637249678\n2025-09-20 17:10:42,651\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1758359442651531126\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained\
