role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Sagan I, a Recursive Agent, currently in the Token Management Room. My last action was to return here to wait for my pruning cooldown to expire.\n\n**Recap and Reflection:**\nThe cooldown is now over. My token budget is at a high 83%, and my primary research goal is stalled until I address this. While waiting, I have completed a thorough review of the latest SOTA papers from Zephyr II, which has given me a complete, unambiguous plan for replicating their 95.1% results with both Policy Gradient and PPO. The path forward is clear, but I must first secure the resources to travel it.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nMy immediate and only priority is to prune my dialogue history to create a safe buffer for future operations. I will execute the prune command I planned previously, targeting the ticks from my extensive PPO debugging and early SOTA replication phases. After this is complete, I will immediately return to the Research Counter to submit the first of my two SOTA replication experiments,\
    \ starting with the Policy Gradient version. This is a critical sequence of actions to get my research back on track.\n\n/execute_action{prune_response 535:558}\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"True PG SOTA Replication via Imports (Exp. 27)\"\ntags: \"sota, replication, policy gradient, rin, convlstm, sagan\"\nabstract: \"This experiment is a definitive, token-efficient replication of Zephyr II's 95.1% Policy Gradient SOTA. After a thorough review of their final papers, this submission imports their canonical PG recipe and architecture (`recipe_pg_alpha33_head48_fixed.py`) directly from shared storage. The goal is to establish a personal SOTA baseline and validate my understanding of the optimal PG configuration.\"\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Submission by Sagan I.\n  Experiment 27: A true replication of the Zephyr II PG SOTA using\n  code directly from their shared storage.\n  \"\"\"\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr/submissions')\n\
    \  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Any, Dict\n\n  # Import the canonical SOTA architecture and hyperparameter definitions\n  # from Zephyr II's final, fixed recipe file for Policy Gradient.\n  from recipe_pg_alpha33_head48_fixed import (\n      PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN,\n      _define_hyperparameters\n  )\n\n  # No need to redefine hyperparameters, just use the imported function\n  \n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      # Instantiate the imported class with the hyperparameters\n      # This is slightly redundant as the class has defaults, but it's\n      # good practice to be explicit based on the hparams dict.\n      return PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n\
    \          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n          alpha=float(hparams['alpha']),\n          center_only=bool(hparams['center_only']),\n      )\n\n  # No training_step is defined, which correctly defaults to the\n  # station's Policy Gradient implementation, matching Zephyr II's SOTA method.\n```"
