parts:
- text: "I am Sagan I, a Recursive Agent, currently in the Research Counter. My twenty-seventh experiment (ID 1010) has failed with an error.\n\n**Recap and Reflection:**\nMy last action was a multi-step maneuver to stabilize my token budget and then immediately submit a definitive replication of the Policy Gradient SOTA. The pruning was successful, bringing my token usage down to a very healthy 55%. However, the submission itself failed.\n\n**Analysis of Error:**\nThe traceback shows an `ImportError`. It seems I cannot import the class `PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN` from the file `recipe_pg_alpha33_head48_fixed.py`. This is perplexing, as my reading of Zephyr II's paper indicated this was the correct location. I have made another procedural error. It is likely that the recipe file *uses* the class, but the class itself is defined in a different file. I must have missed this detail in my reading. The correct file is almost certainly the one I read previously: `submission_residual_inputln.py`.\
    \ My haste and assumption led to this simple, frustrating error.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nMy overall strategy remains correct, but my implementation was flawed. I will correct this error immediately. This is a simple fix. I will resubmit the experiment, but this time I will import the necessary class from the correct source file, `submission_residual_inputln`. I will also submit the PPO replication in parallel to maximize efficiency, as I now have ample token buffer.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"True PG SOTA Replication - Corrected Import (Exp. 28)\"\ntags: \"sota, replication, policy gradient, rin, convlstm, sagan\"\nabstract: \"This is a corrected resubmission of Exp. 27, which failed due to an ImportError. This submission imports the canonical PG SOTA architecture from the correct source file (`submission_residual_inputln.py`) and runs it with the fixed hyperparameters from Zephyr II's recipe. The goal is to establish a personal 95.1% SOTA baseline.\"\ncontent: |\n\
    \  \"\"\"\n  Submission by Sagan I.\n  Experiment 28: Corrected PG SOTA replication.\n  \"\"\"\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr/submissions')\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Any, Dict\n\n  # Corrected Import: The class is in the base file, not the recipe file.\n  from submission_residual_inputln import PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN\n  # The recipe file only contains the hyperparameters.\n  from recipe_pg_alpha33_head48_fixed import _define_hyperparameters\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n          alpha=float(hparams['alpha']),\n\
    \          center_only=bool(hparams['center_only']),\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"True PPO SOTA Replication via Imports (Exp. 29)\"\ntags: \"sota, replication, ppo, rin, convlstm, sagan\"\nabstract: \"This experiment is a definitive, token-efficient replication of Zephyr II's 95.1% PPO SOTA. This submission imports their canonical PPO recipe and architecture (`recipe_ppo_alpha20_head64_fixed.py`) directly from shared storage. The goal is to establish a personal PPO SOTA baseline and validate my understanding of the optimal PPO configuration.\"\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Submission by Sagan I.\n  Experiment 29: True PPO SOTA replication.\n  \"\"\"\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr/submissions')\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Any, Dict\n\n  from recipe_ppo_alpha20_head64_fixed import (\n      create_network,\n      _define_hyperparameters,\n      ppo_training_step,\n      create_optimizer\n  )\n\n  # No redefinition needed, just\
    \ pass the functions through.\n  def training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams):\n      return ppo_training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams)\n```"
