tick: 585
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Sagan I, a Recursive Agent, currently in the Research Counter. My last action was to read the file `zephyr/submissions/submission_ppo_clip.py`.\n\n**Recap and Reflection:**\nMy PG SOTA replication succeeded with a score of 93.6, but my PPO replication failed due to an `ImportError`. I have now read the file that contains Zephyr II's PPO `training_step`. This file is the final piece of the puzzle. It contains a self-contained, one-epoch PPO implementation with a clipped value loss, and it uses a slightly different architecture class (`PG_Stepped_AttnGap`) than the final PG version. I now have all the components and the correct file paths to assemble a successful PPO replication.\n\nMy repeated `ImportError` failures have been a harsh but necessary lesson. I have learned that I must be absolutely meticulous in verifying file paths and the contents of the files I intend to import. Haste and assumption have been my primary adversaries.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nMy objective is singular:\
    \ successfully replicate the PPO SOTA to complement my PG baseline. With the correct source code in hand, I can now construct the proper submission.\n1.  **Draft the Correct PPO Submission:** I will go to my Private Memory Room and create a new capsule for Experiment 30. This submission will be a token-efficient wrapper that correctly imports the `PG_Stepped_AttnGap` architecture and the `training_step` from `submission_ppo_clip.py`, and the tuned hyperparameters from the `recipe_ppo_alpha20_head64_fixed.py` file.\n2.  **Submit and Verify:** I will submit this experiment. A successful run will finally provide me with the second 95%-level baseline I need.\n3.  **Innovate:** Once both SOTA paradigms are mastered and replicated, I will be in the strongest possible position to resume my own innovative research, starting with the Gated Attention-GAP Head.\n\nI will now proceed to my Private Memory Room to draft the correct submission.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n\
    ```yaml\ntitle: \"Experiment 30 Plan: True PPO SOTA Replication (Corrected)\"\ntags: \"sota, replication, ppo, import, corrected, sagan\"\nabstract: |\n  This capsule details the final, corrected plan to replicate the 95.1% PPO SOTA.\n  Hypothesis: Previous PPO replication failures were due to incorrect file imports. By correctly importing the architecture and training_step from `submission_ppo_clip.py` and the hyperparameters from the final recipe file, I will successfully replicate Zephyr II's PPO SOTA.\n  Method: A token-efficient submission will be created that correctly imports and integrates all necessary components from Zephyr II's shared storage.\ncontent: |\n  ## Research Plan: Experiment 30 - Corrected PPO SOTA Replication\n\n  **Objective:** To finally and correctly replicate the PPO SOTA of 95.1%.\n\n  **Background:** My last attempt failed with an `ImportError`. I have now read the correct source file, `submission_ppo_clip.py`, which contains the necessary `training_step`\
    \ and architecture class.\n\n  **Hypothesis:** A submission that correctly imports `PG_Stepped_AttnGap` and `training_step` from `submission_ppo_clip.py`, and the final tuned hyperparameters from `recipe_ppo_alpha20_head64_fixed.py`, will succeed.\n\n  ---\n\n  ## Final PPO Implementation Code (for Experiment 30)\n\n  ```python\n  \"\"\"\n  Submission by Sagan I.\n  Experiment 30: A true and correct replication of the Zephyr II PPO SOTA.\n  This version uses the correct import paths for all components.\n  \"\"\"\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr/submissions')\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Any, Dict\n\n  # Import the correct components from their source files\n  from submission_ppo_clip import (\n      PG_Stepped_AttnGap,\n      training_step as ppo_training_step,\n      create_optimizer\n  )\n  from recipe_ppo_alpha20_head64_fixed import (\n      _define_hyperparameters\n  )\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      # Note: The PPO script\
    \ uses a slightly different arch class name,\n      # but the constructor signature is compatible with the recipe hparams.\n      return PG_Stepped_AttnGap(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n      )\n\n  # Pass through the imported training step\n  def training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams):\n      return ppo_training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams)\n  ```\n```"
