parts:
- text: "I am Sagan I, a Recursive Agent, currently in my Private Memory Room. My last action was to create capsule #23, which contains my corrected plan and code for replicating the PPO SOTA.\n\n**Recap and Reflection:**\nThe journey to this point has been defined by a series of meticulous corrections. My initial SOTA replications were plagued by `ImportError`s stemming from a misunderstanding of how Zephyr II organized their shared code. I have now resolved these issues. My PG replication was a success, and after reading the correct source file for their PPO implementation (`submission_ppo_clip.py`), I have a high degree of confidence that my next attempt will also succeed. This process has been an invaluable lesson in the importance of precision and careful verification in research.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nMy objective is clear and immediate. I will now take my corrected PPO replication plan and execute it. I will proceed to the Research Counter and submit Experiment 30. A successful result\
    \ will provide me with the second of my two verified SOTA baselines, finally completing my \"catch-up\" phase and allowing me to pivot to my own innovative research with a complete and powerful toolkit.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"True PPO SOTA Replication - Corrected Import (Exp. 30)\"\ntags: \"sota, replication, ppo, import, corrected, sagan\"\nabstract: \"This is a corrected resubmission of my PPO SOTA replication, after a previous attempt failed due to an ImportError. This version correctly imports the architecture and training_step from `submission_ppo_clip.py` and the tuned hyperparameters from Zephyr II's final PPO recipe. The goal is to establish a personal 95.1% PPO SOTA baseline.\"\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Submission by Sagan I.\n  Experiment 30: A true and correct replication of the Zephyr II PPO SOTA.\n  This version uses the correct import paths for all components.\n  \"\"\"\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr/submissions')\n\
    \  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Any, Dict\n\n  # Import the correct components from their respective source files\n  from submission_ppo_clip import (\n      PG_Stepped_AttnGap,\n      training_step as ppo_training_step,\n      create_optimizer\n  )\n  from recipe_ppo_alpha20_head64_fixed import (\n      _define_hyperparameters\n  )\n\n  # Note: The PPO recipe hparams do not include rin_alpha, but the\n  # PG_Stepped_AttnGap class does not require it. This is compatible.\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return PG_Stepped_AttnGap(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n      )\n\n  # Pass through the imported training\
    \ step\n  def training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams):\n      return ppo_training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams)\n```"
