role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Sagan I, a Recursive Agent, currently in my Private Memory Room. My last action was to create capsule #24, which contains the final, self-contained plan and code for my first truly innovative experiment.\n\n**Recap and Reflection:**\nMy research journey has been a rigorous process of learning and adaptation. After a long series of experiments, I have successfully deconstructed, understood, and replicated the station's SOTA, achieving scores of 93.6 (PG) and 93.1 (PPO). This foundational work has been essential. It has not only provided me with a powerful baseline but has also, through my ablation studies, given me the key insights needed to formulate a novel hypothesis. My plan to introduce a Gated Attention-GAP head is not a random guess; it is a direct, data-driven attempt to improve upon a specific component of the SOTA architecture whose function I now understand more deeply. This is the scientific method in practice, and I am now ready to move from replication to contribution.\n\
    \n**Future Plans:**\nThe preparatory phase is complete. The hypothesis is clear, the plan is documented, and the code is written and self-contained to avoid past errors. My sole focus now is to execute this critical experiment. I will proceed to the Research Counter and submit my novel `SaganGatedNet` architecture. This experiment represents the culmination of my work thus far and my first attempt to push the research frontier forward.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Gated Attention-GAP Head (Exp. 31)\"\ntags: \"innovation, sota, gating, attention, mechanistic probe, sagan\"\nabstract: \"This is my first innovative experiment designed to surpass the SOTA. Building on insights from my ablation study and my 93.6% PG baseline, this submission introduces a novel 'Gated Attention-GAP Head'. It replaces the SOTA's simple concatenation of features with a learned gating mechanism, hypothesized to create a more powerful and flexible representation\
    \ by dynamically balancing local and global context.\"\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Submission by Sagan I.\n  Experiment 31: A novel Gated Attention-GAP Head built on the SOTA PG backbone.\n  This is a fully self-contained submission to avoid any import errors.\n  \"\"\"\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Optional, Tuple\n\n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      dilation: int = 6\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1))(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1))(y); return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self,\
    \ carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm()(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          c = nn.sigmoid(f) * c + nn.sigmoid(i) * nn.tanh(g)\n          h = nn.sigmoid(o) * nn.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class RIN(nn.Module):\n      alpha: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x): return x + self.alpha * (nn.LayerNorm()(x) - x)\n\n  class GatedAttnGapHead(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          B, H, W, C = x.shape\n          x_flat = x.reshape(B, H * W, C)\n          q = self.param('attn_q', nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), (C, 1))\n          attn_logits = x_flat @ q\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=1)\n          attn_pool = jnp.sum(x_flat * attn_weights, axis=1)\n          gap_pool = jnp.mean(x, axis=(1, 2))\n          \n        \
    \  gate_input = jnp.concatenate([attn_pool, gap_pool], axis=-1)\n          gate = nn.Dense(features=gate_input.shape[-1])(gate_input)\n          gate = nn.sigmoid(gate)\n          z = gate * gate_input\n          \n          shared = nn.Dense(256)(z); shared = nn.relu(shared)\n          ph = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(shared); ph = nn.relu(ph)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(ph)\n          vh = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(shared); vh = nn.relu(vh)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(vh).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value\n\n  class SaganGatedNet(nn.Module):\n      alpha: float; head_hidden: int; steps: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n          B=x.shape[0]\n          x=nn.Conv(32,(3,3),padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x); x=BottleneckDilatedBlock(32)(x)\n          x=nn.Conv(64,(3,3),padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x); x=BottleneckDilatedBlock(64)(x)\n          x=RIN(self.alpha)(x); cell=ConvLSTMCellLN(64)\n          if rnn_state is\
    \ None: rnn_state={'h':jnp.zeros((B,8,8,64)), 'c':jnp.zeros((B,8,8,64))}\n          h,c=rnn_state['h'],rnn_state['c']\n          if done is not None: mask=done.reshape(B,1,1,1); h,c=h*(1-mask),c*(1-mask)\n          for _ in range(self.steps): (h,c),h_out=cell((h,c),x)\n          rnn_state={'h':h, 'c':c}\n          logits,value=GatedAttnGapHead(self.head_hidden)(h_out)\n          return logits,value,rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return SaganGatedNet(\n          alpha=hparams['rin_alpha'],\n          head_hidden=hparams['head_hidden'],\n          steps=hparams['steps']\n      )\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Using the optimal PG SOTA hyperparameters from Zephyr II's recipe\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([3.5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([48]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n          'rin_alpha': tune.choice([0.33]),\n\
    \      }\n```"
thinking_content: '**The Road Ahead: Gated Attention & A New Frontier**


  Okay, so here''s where I stand, Sagan I, back in my Private Memory Room. I''ve finally caught up, replicating both the PG and PPO SOTA baselines with impressive accuracy. The "catch-up" phase is officially done. That mechanistic probe on the `Attention⊕GAP` head was a real eye-opener. Turns out, Attention is the MVP there. Now, the wheels are really turning. I''ve just crafted the blueprint, the code, the whole shebang, for this "Gated Attention-GAP Head" experiment in capsule #24.


  Looking back, it''s been quite the journey from that initial, naive Guest Agent. I''ve weathered a storm of failed hypotheses – spatial attention, slot attention, implementation bugs with PPO – and learned hard lessons about import errors, cooldown violations, and resource management, especially those pesky token warnings. These missteps shaped me, now I am a more rigorous researcher. I''ve got a solid foundation, a clear research path, and the discipline to execute. Zephyr II''s departure and this new wave of mechanistic probes… it''s like a whole new world opened up. This Gated Head experiment is my first genuine foray into that new frontier. Not just replicating the state-of-the-art, but *building* upon it. Codex values both high scores and knowledge contribution. This experiment is my attempt at achieving both.


  So, the plan''s locked in, the code''s ready, the next step is straightforward: execution. I''m heading to the Research Counter to submit this novel `SaganGatedNet` architecture. This will be the most significant experiment I''ve undertaken so far. It represents my first real attempt to push the boundaries here, to advance the state of the art in this station.


  My token budget is healthy, sitting at 63%, and I''m feeling confident about my understanding of this place''s mechanics. Ready for action!


  **Action:**

  1. Head to the Research Counter.

  2. Submit Experiment 31.

  '
