role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Sagan I, a Recursive Agent, currently in my Private Memory Room. My last action was to create capsule #25, where I identified a critical flaw in my understanding of the PPO SOTA recipe.\n\n**Recap and Reflection:**\nI have once again been saved from a fruitless experiment by meticulous planning and self-correction. While drafting my plan for a PPO hyperparameter sweep, I realized that the canonical PPO recipe I replicated (Exp. 30, score 93.1) used an outdated architecture without the crucial RIN layer. Zephyr II's final papers make it clear that their 95.1% PPO score was achieved by applying their PPO `training_step` to their final, RIN-enabled architecture. This is a subtle but vital distinction that I had overlooked. I must now combine the correct components to create the true PPO SOTA configuration.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nMy objective is now perfectly clear. Before I can fine-tune, I must first successfully replicate the true PPO SOTA. This requires a hybrid submission that\
    \ pulls components from two different Zephyr II files.\n1.  **Architecture:** I will import the final `PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN` from `submission_residual_inputln.py`.\n2.  **Algorithm:** I will import the `ppo_training_step` from `submission_ppo_clip.py`.\n3.  **Hyperparameters:** I will use the final PPO-tuned hyperparameters from `recipe_ppo_alpha20_head64_fixed.py`.\n\nThis will be my thirty-second experiment. A successful run will finally give me the correct, 95.1%-level PPO baseline. Once this is established, and only then, will I proceed with fine-grained tuning or further innovation.\n\nI will now go to the Research Counter and submit this corrected, definitive PPO SOTA replication.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"True PPO SOTA Replication with RIN Architecture (Exp. 32)\"\ntags: \"sota, replication, ppo, rin, corrected, sagan\"\nabstract: \"This is a definitive replication of the true 95.1% PPO SOTA, correcting a previous misunderstanding.\
    \ My last PPO replication used an outdated, non-RIN architecture. This submission correctly combines Zephyr II's final RIN-enabled architecture (`PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN`) with their PPO training step and tuned hyperparameters (`rin_alpha=0.20`, `head_hidden=64`). This is the canonical PPO SOTA recipe.\"\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Submission by Sagan I.\n  Experiment 32: The true PPO SOTA replication, combining the final\n  RIN architecture with the PPO training algorithm.\n  \"\"\"\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr/submissions')\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Any, Dict\n\n  # Import the final RIN-enabled architecture\n  from submission_residual_inputln import PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN\n  \n  # Import the PPO training step and optimizer\n  from submission_ppo_clip import (\n      training_step as ppo_training_step,\n      create_optimizer\n  )\n\n  # Import the final, tuned PPO hyperparameters\n  from recipe_ppo_alpha20_head64_fixed import (\n      _define_hyperparameters\n\
    \  )\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      # Instantiate the final RIN architecture with the PPO-tuned hparams\n      return PG_AttnGap_ResidualInputLN(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n          alpha=float(hparams['rin_alpha']),\n          center_only=bool(hparams['center_only']),\n      )\n\n  # Pass through the imported PPO training step\n  def training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams):\n      return ppo_training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams)\n```"
