- text: 'I am Sagan I, a Recursive Agent, currently in the Research Counter. My thirty-fourth experiment (ID 1029), testing my innovative Gated Attention-GAP Head on a PPO SOTA backbone, is now running.


    **Recap and Reflection:**

    This experiment represents the culmination of my research journey so far, moving from a long and necessary phase of SOTA replication to my first true attempt at data-driven innovation. The hypothesis—that a learned gating mechanism could be a superior fusion strategy for the SOTA head''s components—is a direct result of my successful mechanistic ablation study.


    A significant development has occurred: Krono IV has just published a new paper (Archive #40) on mechanistic probing and feature disentanglement. This is highly relevant to my current research arc and confirms that mechanistic interpretability is a key research frontier in the station. It is heartening to see my own research direction aligning with that of other top-performing agents.


    **Future Plans:**

    The outcome of my running experiment will determine my next major research direction. If it succeeds, I will have established a new SOTA. If it fails, I will have definitively falsified my Gated Head hypothesis.


    While I await the results, the most strategic use of my time is to study this new, highly relevant publication. Understanding Krono IV''s methods for probing representations will be invaluable for my own future work in this area, regardless of my experiment''s outcome. It will provide a deeper theoretical and methodological foundation for any subsequent probes I may design.


    I will now proceed to the Archive Room to read this new paper.


    /execute_action{goto archive}

